  <para style="h">Mme Abiideikpe</para>
  <para style="toc1">Mme Abiideikpe</para>
  <para style="toc2">Mme Abiideikpe</para>
  <para style="toc3">Abi</para>
  <para style="mt1">Mme Abiideikpe</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="JDG 1" />
  <para style="s1">Nditọ Isrel Enwana ye Nsʌhọ Mbon Kenan</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JDG 1:1" />Ke Yọsua amaakekpa, nditọ Isrel emaebịp <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, “Anie ke atu ñnyịn idiido akpa awo se idọọk ikaa ikinwana ye mbon Kenan?”<verse eid="JDG 1:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="JDG 1:2" />
    <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaabọọrọ, “Yuda ayaadọọk akaa; ami mme yaak isọñ ado nsịn ammọ ke ubọk.”<verse eid="JDG 1:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="JDG 1:3" />Ideen Yuda emaebo mbon Simiọn e-edooho emọ-emọ mbon Isrel, “Idi yak ñnyịn idọọk ika ke udeeme isọñ ekinọọhọ ñnyịn, ikinwana ye mbon Kenan. Ñnyịn ñko iyainyʌñ ikeene ndufo ikaa ake ndufo.” Akema nditọ Simiọn emaekeene ammọ ekaa.<verse eid="JDG 1:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="JDG 1:4" />Ke ini Yuda akenwanake, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaayaak mbon Kenan ye mbon Peris asịn ammọ ke ubọk, ndin ammọ emaewoot ideen tọsịn duob (10,000) ke Besek. <verse eid="JDG 1:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JDG 1:5" />Ke itie ado ke ammọ ekekịt Adọni-Besek enyʌñ enwana ye anye, esịn nsobo ye mbon Kenan ye mbon Peris. <verse eid="JDG 1:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JDG 1:6" />Adọni-Besek amaafeghe, ado ammọ emaebịne anye enyʌñ ekemʌm anye, enyʌñ ekpok mme akpan nnuunubọk ye mme akpan nnuunukod amọ.<verse eid="JDG 1:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="JDG 1:7" />Akema Adọni-Besek amaabo, “Ndidem ata mme duob e-ekekpịkkeke akpan nnuunubọk ye akpan nnuunukod ammọ esio emaetañ mbeñe ke idak akpokoro mmi. Idahami Abasi ansio miin usiene ke se ami ñkenam ye ammọ.” Ammọ emaeben anye edi ke Yeruselem, ndin anye amaakpa do.<verse eid="JDG 1:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="JDG 1:8" />Mme ideen Yuda emaekenwana ye Yeruselem enyʌñ edat enie. Ammọ emaesịn akañkañ ke abio ado enyʌñ ekịm ikañ.<verse eid="JDG 1:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="JDG 1:9" />Ke ado amaakeboiyo, Yuda amaasọiyọ akaa akenwana ye mbon Kenan e-ekedʌñọke ke abio abod-abod, ke Nekef ye unaisọñ ke ñkañ usobutịn. <verse eid="JDG 1:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JDG 1:10" />Mbon Yuda emaenyʌñ ekaa ekenwana ye mbon Kenan e-ekedʌñọke ke Hibrọn (e-ekesikoodo Kiriad Aaba) enyʌñ ekan Sesai, Ahiman ye Talmai. <verse eid="JDG 1:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JDG 1:11" />Ammọ emaeto do ekaa ebịne mbon e-ekedʌñọke ke Debi (e-ekesikoodo Kiriad Sefa).<verse eid="JDG 1:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="JDG 1:12" />Ndin Kaleb amaabo ate, “Ami ñyaanọ awo adiinwana inyʌñ ikan Kiriad Sefa ayịn awonwaan mmi Aksa ke ndọ.” <verse eid="JDG 1:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JDG 1:13" />Otniel ayịn Kenas, etək ayịneka Kaleb, adat anye; ndin Kaleb amaanọ anye ayịn awonwaan amọ Aksa ke ndọ.<verse eid="JDG 1:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="JDG 1:14" />Usen keed ke ini Aksa akediighe abịne Otniel, anye amaanyịk anye ate yak abeeñe ete imọ inwañ. Ke ini anye amaakesọiyọ ke dọñki amọ, Kaleb amaabịp Aksa ate, “Nsoo ke ami ñkeme adinam unọọ fiin?”<verse eid="JDG 1:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="JDG 1:15" />Anye amaabọọrọ ate, “Fọn asaña asaña mfọn keed ye ami. Sia afo umaukunnọ miin isọñ ke Nekef, nyʌñ nnọ miin mme idịm mmọọñ ñko.” Ndin Kaleb amaanọ anye iso idịm ye usuuk idịm.<verse eid="JDG 1:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="JDG 1:16" />Mbon e-eketooho ubon ete anwaan Moses, mbon Keen, emaeto ke Abio Ayob<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1:16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho Yeriko</char></note> ye mbon Yuda ekaa edikidʌñ ke atu mbon e-ekedʌñọke ke Akpautatan Yuda ke Nekef a-akpereke Arad.<verse eid="JDG 1:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="JDG 1:17" />Akema mbon Yuda emaekaa ye mbon Simiọn mme nditọete ammọ ke Isrel emaenyʌñ ekenwana ye mbon Kenan e-edʌñọke ke Sefad, ammọ emaenyʌñ esobo abio ado afịd-afịd. Ado anam ekekoot anye Họma.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1:17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Họma awuọñọ nsobo</char></note> <verse eid="JDG 1:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JDG 1:18" />Yuda amaanyʌñ adat Kasa, Askelọn ye Ekrọn, abio keedekeed ye adaña amọ.<verse eid="JDG 1:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="JDG 1:19" />
    <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaaba ye mbon Yuda. Ammọ emaedat abio abod-abod enie, ado ammọ ikikanna ibịne mbon ado isio ke unaisọñ, sia ammọ emaenie sariọd ekeyịtte ukwak. <verse eid="JDG 1:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JDG 1:20" />Naña Moses akenwọñọ, emaeben Hibrọn enọ Kaleb, a-akebịneke nditọ Anak ita asịññe. <verse eid="JDG 1:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JDG 1:21" />Mbon Benyamin, naña akeba, ikibịneke mbon Yebus, e-ekedʌñọke ke Yeruselem; tutu mfịn ami mbon Yebus edʌñọ ke ndo ye mbon Benyamin.<verse eid="JDG 1:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="JDG 1:22" />Ndin mbon esiin Yosef emaenwana ye Beteel, ndin <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaanyʌñ aba ye ammọ. <verse eid="JDG 1:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JDG 1:23" />Ke ini mbon ufọk Yosef ekedọññọ ideen yak ekeyep abio Beteel (e-ekesikoodo Luus), <verse eid="JDG 1:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JDG 1:24" />mbon uyeb emaekịt awodeen keed naña ato esịd abio ado awuọ adi ndin ammọ emaebo anye, “Iwọt ñnyịn naña idisaña idʌk esịd abio ami ndin ñnyịn iyaikịt ibo ke iminam nọ afọn ye afo.” <verse eid="JDG 1:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JDG 1:25" />Ndin anye amaawọt ammọ, ammọ emaenyʌñ esịn akañkañ ke abio ado, ado emaeyaak awo ado ye afịd ubon amọ. <verse eid="JDG 1:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="JDG 1:26" />Akema anye amaadakka akaa isọñ mbon Hed, itie a-anye akebọppọ abio anyʌñ akoot anye Luus, a-adooho anyịñ amọ tutu mfịn.<verse eid="JDG 1:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="JDG 1:27" />Ado Manase ikibịneke mbon Bed San me Taanak me Dọọ me Ibleem me Mekido ye mme ñkanñkʌk ntək abio isọñ, sia mbon Kenan emaesọọñọ enekke eyem edidʌñọ ke isọñ ado. <verse eid="JDG 1:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="JDG 1:28" />Ke ini Isrel amaakenekke asọñ idem, ammọ emaefiik mbon Kenan esịn ke adinam akpọsọñ utom ufen ado ikibịneke ammọ isịññe afịd-afịd. <verse eid="JDG 1:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="JDG 1:29" />Ifrem ikinyʌññọ ibịne mbon Kenan e-ekedʌñọke ke Kesa isịññe, ado mbon Kenan emaekaa iso edʌñọ ke atu ammọ. <verse eid="JDG 1:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="JDG 1:30" />Sebulọn ikibịneke mbon Kenan e-ekedʌñọke ke Kitrọn me Nahalol isịññe, ndin mbon Kenan ado ekedʌñọ ye ammọ, ado Sebulọn amaasịn ammọ ke akpọsọñ utom. <verse eid="JDG 1:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="JDG 1:31" />Asaa ikinyʌññọ ibịne mbon e-ekedʌñọke ke Akko me ke Sidọn me ke Alab me ke Aksịb me ke Helba me ke Afek me ke Rehob isịññe. <verse eid="JDG 1:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="JDG 1:32" />Mbon Asaa ekedʌñọ ke atu mbon Kenan ekedʌñọke ke isọñ ado sia ammọ ikibịneke ammọ isioño. <verse eid="JDG 1:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="JDG 1:33" />Mbon Naftali ikinyʌññọ ibịne mbon ekedʌñọke ke Bed Semes me ke Bed Anad; ado mbon Naftali ñko ekedʌñọ ke atu mbon Kenan ekedʌñọke ke isọñ ado, ndin mbon ekedʌñọke ke Bed Semes ye Bed Anad ekanna edoñño mbon unam utom ufen nnọọ ammọ. <verse eid="JDG 1:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="JDG 1:34" />Mbon Amọọ emaenək mbon Daan esịn ke abod-abod abio, iyakka ammọ esọiyọ edi ke unaisọñ. <verse eid="JDG 1:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="JDG 1:35" />Ndin mbon Amọọ emaenekke esọọñọ eda adimʌm Abod Heres ñkama, Aiyalọn ye Saalbịm, ado ke ini adudu esiin Yosef akemaanake akpon, emaefiik ammọ ñko ke adinam akpọsọñ utom ufen. <verse eid="JDG 1:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="JDG 1:36" />Adaña mbon Amọọ aketọọñọ ke Usʌñ Ikpeyen tutu akewuọ ke Sela anyʌñ aboiyo.<verse eid="JDG 1:36" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JDG 1" />
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="JDG 2" />
  <para style="s1">Enyere <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke Bokịm</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JDG 2:1" />Akem enyere <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadakka ke Kilkal adọọk akaa ke Bokịm anyʌñ akebo, “Ami ñkisịññe ndufo ke Iyib ñnyʌñ idat ndufo ndisịn ke isọñ a-ami ñkenwọñọke adinọ mme eteete ndufo. Ami ñkebo, ‘Tutu amama, ami ndiibiatta edioomo mmi ye ndufo, <verse eid="JDG 2:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JDG 2:2" />ndin inaaha nte ndufo enam edioomo ye mbon idʌñ ami, ado ana ndufo ewuut mme akpokoro uwa ammọ.’ Ado ndufo emaetre utọñ ye ami. Ntak a-ndufo enamma ntom-o? <verse eid="JDG 2:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JDG 2:3" />Ndin ami mmaanyʌñ mbo, ‘Ami ndiibịneke ammọ nsio ke iso ndufo; ammọ eyaedoñño afia inọ ndufo, mme abasi ammọ eyaenyʌñ edoñño mfịna inọ ndufo.’ ”<verse eid="JDG 2:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="JDG 2:4" />Ke ini enyere <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaaketañ mme ñkpọ ami anọ afịd mbon Isrel, ammọ emaebenne uyio etua ayịd, <verse eid="JDG 2:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JDG 2:5" />ndin ammọ emaekoot itie ado Bokịm.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2:5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Bokịm awuọñọ mme atua ayịd</char></note> Ke itie ado ammọ emaewa uwa enọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.<verse eid="JDG 2:5" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ntịdutọñ ye Iduọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="JDG 2:6" />Ke Yọsua amaakesuan mbon Isrel, ammọ emaedakka ekaa adikidat isọñ ado nnie, ammọ keedekeed emaekaa itie udeeme ammọ. <verse eid="JDG 2:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JDG 2:7" />Mbon ami emaenam ñkpọ enọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke afịd ayio uwem Yọsua ye ake mme ñkpisọñ e-ekekpeeneke uwem ekan anye e-ekenyʌññọ ekiit afịd ikpọ ñkpọ se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> akenam anọ Isrel.<verse eid="JDG 2:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="JDG 2:8" />Yọsua ayịn Nọn, ayịnufọk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, amaakpa ke ini anye akesọññọ isua ikie mme duob. <verse eid="JDG 2:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JDG 2:9" />Ndin ammọ emaebuuk anye ke udeeme isọñ ammọ, ke Timnad Heres<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2:9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Enyʌñ ediọọñọ nte Timnad Sera (se ke Yọsua 19:50 ye 24:30)</char></note> ke abio abod-abod ke Ifrem, anyọñ-anyọñ ukañ abod Kaas.<verse eid="JDG 2:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="JDG 2:10" />Ke afịd emana ado emaekebọ nduọkadudu ye mme eteete ammọ, emana mfen amaatịppe a-mmiikidiọọñọke <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> me se anye akenam anọ Isrel. <verse eid="JDG 2:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JDG 2:11" />Akema nditọ Isrel emaenam idiọọkñkpọ ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> emaenyʌñ ekpono mme Baal. <verse eid="JDG 2:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JDG 2:12" />Ammọ emaesịn <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, Abasi mme eteete ammọ, a-akesioho ammọ ke Iyib. Ammọ emaekeene enyʌñ ekpono nsio-nsio abasi mbon e-ekannake ammọ ekʌk. Ammọ ndin emaedemme iyadesịd <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> <verse eid="JDG 2:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JDG 2:13" />sia ammọ ekesịnne Abọọñ enyʌñ enam ñkpọ enọ Baal ye mme Astọred. <verse eid="JDG 2:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JDG 2:14" />Ke iyadesịd ami ye Isrel <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaayaak ammọ asịn ke ubọk mbon mbịme e-ekesuanna ammọ. Anye amaanyam ammọ asịn ke ubọk mme asua ke afịd ñkanñkʌk, a-ammọ imiikidikanna aba ke anwan. <verse eid="JDG 2:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JDG 2:15" />Ini keed akeedodo Isrel akekaaha anwan, ubọk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ikibaaha ye ammọ ndin emaekan ammọ, kpa naña anye akenwọñọ anọ ammọ. Ammọ ekeba ke ekamba mfiomo.<verse eid="JDG 2:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="JDG 2:16" />Akema <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaasio mme abiideikpe,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2:16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Akeme ido mme adaiwuod; se ñko ke Ñwed Mme Abiideikpe 2:17-19</char></note> e-ekenyaañake ammọ esio ke ubọk mbon mbịme. <verse eid="JDG 2:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JDG 2:17" />Ado ammọ ikikpañña utọñ inọ mme abiideikpe ami, utu ke ado ammọ emaenam akpara ye mme isen abasi enyʌñ ekpono ammọ. Ammọ emaesọsọp ewọññọ iso ekpọñ usʌñ mme eteete ammọ, e-ekesuuhọ iwuod enọ ewʌhọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. <verse eid="JDG 2:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JDG 2:18" />Ini keed akeedodo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> akesioho abiideikpe anọ ammọ, anye amaaba ye abiideikpe ado anyʌñ anyaaña ammọ asio ke ubọk mme asua adaña nte abiideikpe ado aduuho uwem, sia <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ikiduọkkọ adudu ke ntak aseeme ammọ ke idak mbon e-ekefiighe e-ekenyʌññọ esịn ammọ ke ukuud. <verse eid="JDG 2:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JDG 2:19" />Ado abiideikpe ado amaakpa, mbon awo emaetịmme ekaa mme usʌñ a-akenekkeke adiọọk akan ake mme eteete ammọ, ke adikeene mme abasi mfen ñnyʌñ nnam ñkpọ nnọọ ammọ, ñnyʌñ ñkpono ammọ. Ammọ emaesịn edisaana mme ndiọi adinam ye nsọñiwuod ammọ ñyaak.<verse eid="JDG 2:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="JDG 2:20" />Ndin <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaayat esịd ataa eti-eti ye Isrel anyʌñ abo, “Sia idịd ami emaebiat edioomo a-ami ñke anamma nnọ mme eteete ammọ ndin inyʌññọ ikpañ utọñ innọ miin, <verse eid="JDG 2:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JDG 2:21" />ami ndiibịneke aba mme idịd ake Yọsua akekpaaha akpọñ nsịññe ke iso ammọ. <verse eid="JDG 2:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JDG 2:22" />Ami ñyaadat ammọ ndomo Isrel idomo nse me ammọ eyaekeene usʌñ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> enyʌñ esaña ke anye kpa naña mme eteete ammọ ekenam.” <verse eid="JDG 2:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JDG 2:23" /><char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaayaak mme idịd ado esʌhọ; anye ikibịneke ammọ isịññe ini keed ke adiyaak ammọ nsịn ke ubọk Yọsua.<verse eid="JDG 2:23" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JDG 2" />
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="JDG 3" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JDG 3:1" />Mbon ami ado mme idịd se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> akekpọñ nọ edomo afịd mbon Isrel imiikinieghe ifiọk ibaña mme ekọñ ke Kenan <verse eid="JDG 3:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JDG 3:2" />(anye akenam ami adikpeep mbon ubon Isrel i-imiikinieghe ifiọk ibaña ekọñ naña ekeme adinwana ekọñ): <verse eid="JDG 3:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JDG 3:3" />Mme andikara ition ke Filistia, afịd mbon Kenan, mbon Sidọn, ye mbon Hif e-ekedʌñọke ke mme abod Lebanọn eto ke abod Baal Hemọn ekaa ke Lebo Hamad. <verse eid="JDG 3:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JDG 3:4" />Ekekpọñ ammọ nọ edomo mbon Isrel ese me ammọ eyaesuuk iwuod enọ mme mbed <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, a-anye akenọọhọ mme eteete ammọ ke ubọk Moses.<verse eid="JDG 3:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="JDG 3:5" />Mbon Isrel ekedʌñọ ke atu mbon Kenan, mbon Hed, Amọọ, Peris, mbon Hif ye mbon Yebus. <verse eid="JDG 3:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JDG 3:6" />Ammọ emaekoono nditọ ibaan ammọ edọ enyʌñ eben nditọ ibaan ammọ enọ nditọ ideen ammọ, enyʌñ enam ñkpọ enọ mme abasi ammọ.<verse eid="JDG 3:6" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Otniel</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="JDG 3:7" />Mbon Isrel emaenam idiọọkñkpọ ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>; ammọ emaefre <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi ammọ enyʌñ enam ñkpọ enọ mme Baal ye mme Asera. <verse eid="JDG 3:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JDG 3:8" />Iyadesịd <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaasak nte ikañ abaña Isrel ndin anye amaanyam ammọ asịn ke ubọk Kusan-Risataim adidem ke Aram Naharaim,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3:8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho Adoro usobutịn Mesopotemia</char></note> a-mbon Isrel ekesịneke ke idak enam ñkpọ enọ ke isua itiaita. <verse eid="JDG 3:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JDG 3:9" />Ado ke ini ammọ eketuaha ekoot <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, anye amaasio andinyaaña anọ mbon Isrel, Otniel ayịn Kenas, etək ayịneka awodeen Kaleb, a-akenyaañake ammọ. <verse eid="JDG 3:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JDG 3:10" />Sịbidịd <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadoro anye ke idem, ndin anye amaakappa ado abiideikpe<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3:10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Me adaiwuod</char></note> ke Isrel anyʌñ akaa ekọñ. <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaaben Kusan-Risataim adidem ke Aram asịn ke ubọk Otniel, a-akekanna anye. <verse eid="JDG 3:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JDG 3:11" />Ndin isọñ amaanie emem ke isua aba, tutu Otniel ayịn Kenas akpa.<verse eid="JDG 3:11" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ehud</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="JDG 3:12" />Ini keed mfen mbon Isrel emaetịmme enam idiọọkñkpọ ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, ndin ke ntak a-ammọ ekenamma idiọọkñkpọ ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaanọ Eklọn adidem ke Mọb adudu adikan Isrel. <verse eid="JDG 3:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JDG 3:13" />Eklọn amaanam mbon Amọn ye mbon Amalek nọ ediana ye anye, ediinwana ye Isrel, enyʌñ eben Abio Ayob<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3:13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho Yeriko</char></note> enie. <verse eid="JDG 3:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JDG 3:14" />Mbon Isrel emaesịne ke idak Eklọn adidem Mọb enam ñkpọ enọ ke isua duob mme itiaita.<verse eid="JDG 3:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="JDG 3:15" />Ini keed mfen mbon Isrel emaetua enọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, anye amaanyʌñ anọ ammọ andinyaaña, Ehud, atufiin, ayịn Kera aketooho ubon Benyamin. Mbon Isrel emaedọñ anye aben utịb ammọ adat asọk Eklọn adidem Mọb. <verse eid="JDG 3:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JDG 3:16" />Ndin Ehud amaanam akañkañ anie iso iba a-akedooho ñkpọ nte kubid keed<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3:16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ñkpọ nte sentimita 45</char></note> ke unyọọñ, a-anye akebọppọ adian ke ifʌkkọ nnasia ke idak afọñ ammọ. <verse eid="JDG 3:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JDG 3:17" />Anye amaaben etob akaa akenọ Eklọn adidem Mọb, a-akedooho ataa akponubom awo. <verse eid="JDG 3:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JDG 3:18" />Ke Ehud amaakenọ utịb ado, anye amaasio mbon se ikiben utịb ado idi unyọñ. <verse eid="JDG 3:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JDG 3:19" />Ado ke anye amaakewuọ itie mme ubobod itiad a-akpereke Kilkal anye ke idem amọ amaatịmme edem abịne Eklọn anyʌñ akebo anye, “Ke Ukpono Adidem, ami mmenie ndedịbe etob adunọọ fiin.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 3:19">Ndin adidem amaabo nditọufọk amọ, “Inọ ñnyịn ufañ!” Ndin afịd ammọ emaewuọñọ.<verse eid="JDG 3:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="JDG 3:20" />Akema Ehud amaasaña akpere anye ke ini anye aketieghe ikpọọñ ke esịd ubeed ke anyọñ ebekpo amọ anyʌñ abo anye, “Ami mmenie etob a-atooho Abasi unọ fiin.” <verse eid="JDG 3:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JDG 3:21" />Ehud amaanyan ubọk ufiin amọ, adʌt akañkañ ke ifʌkkọ nnasia amọ anyʌñ akịm idịb adidem. <verse eid="JDG 3:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JDG 3:22" />Ukeed itoikwa ye isoikwa emaetịkke edʌk anye idịb, ndin ekpa amọ amaawuọñọ. Ehud ikidʌttọ akañkañ ado isio, ndin akpọñ amaafʌk akañkañ. <verse eid="JDG 3:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JDG 3:23" />Akema Ehud amaawuọ adi ke nsañandʌk ufọk, abet mme usʌñ ubeed anyọñ anyʌñ ayịt ammọ.<verse eid="JDG 3:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="JDG 3:24" />Ke anye amaakenyọñ, nditọufọk emaedi enyʌñ edikịt usʌñ ubeed nte ayeyịre. Ammọ emaebo, “Ana ado anye akeñ idem ke esịd ubeed ufọk adidem.” <verse eid="JDG 3:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JDG 3:25" />Ammọ emaebet tutu awuọ ini idem akebọkkọke ammọ, ado ke ini anye imiikiibeereke usʌñ ubeed, ammọ emaeben ñyịn ukpọhọde etat mme usʌñ ado. Ke ndo ke ammọ ekekịt abọọñ ammọ nte amaakeduọ ana ke isọñ akpa.<verse eid="JDG 3:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="JDG 3:26" />Ke ini ammọ ekesʌkkọ ebet do, Ehud amaawuọ anyọñ. Anye amaasaña abọhọ mme ubobod itiad anyʌñ afeghe anyọñ Seira. <verse eid="JDG 3:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="JDG 3:27" />Anye akekewuọ udo, anye amaafịt adukpoñ ke abod-abod abio Ifrem, ndin mbon Isrel emaesọiyọ ye anye eto ke mme abod, ke ini anye akeboiyoke iso anọ ammọ.<verse eid="JDG 3:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="JDG 3:28" />Anye amaanọ uyio ate, “Iñkeene miin, sia Abọọñ a-aben Mọb, asua ndufo, isịn ndufo ke ubọk.” Ndin ammọ emaekeene anye esọiyọ enyʌñ ekeben itịkke Yọdan a-akesañake adʌk Mọb edat enie; ammọ ikiyakka awo ndomokeed afrọ aboiyo. <verse eid="JDG 3:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="JDG 3:29" />Ke ini ado ammọ emaewot mbon Mọb ñkpọ nte tọsịn duob (10,000), afịd ekedo mbon adudu ye ñkpọsọñ awo; ndomo awo keed ikibọkkọke. <verse eid="JDG 3:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="JDG 3:30" />Tọọñọ ke usen ado emaenam Mọb asịne ke idak Isrel, ndin isọñ anie emem ke isua anaañ.<verse eid="JDG 3:30" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Samka</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="JDG 3:31" />Ke Ehud amaakema, Samka ayịn Anad amaawoot mbon Filistia ikie itiokeed (600) ke ikwa uwodenañ. Anye ñko amaanyaaña Isrel.<verse eid="JDG 3:31" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JDG 3" />
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="JDG 4" />
  <para style="s1">Debọra</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JDG 4:1" />Akañ mfen mbon Isrel emaenam idiọọkñkpọ ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, ke Ehud amaakekpa. <verse eid="JDG 4:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JDG 4:2" />Ndin <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaayaak ammọ asịn ke ubọk Yabịn adidem Kenan, a-akekarake ke Hasọ. Sisera, adaiso ekọñ amọ, akedʌñ ke Harosed Hakoyịm. <verse eid="JDG 4:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JDG 4:3" />Sia anye amaanie sariọd ikie usʌkkeed (900) e-ekedatta ukwak enam akenyʌñ afiik mbon Isrel ibak-ibak ke isua edịb, ammọ emaeseeme enọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> eyem unwam.<verse eid="JDG 4:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="JDG 4:4" />Ndin Debọra, a-akedooho prọfed, anwaan Lapidod, akedat<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4:4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Akekpe ikpe</char></note> Isrel usʌñ ke ini ado. <verse eid="JDG 4:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JDG 4:5" />Anye akesinịm esob ke idak Ayob Debọra a-adaaha ke ufọọd Rama ye Beteel ke abio abod-abod Ifrem, ndin mbon Isrel emaesidọọk ekaa ebịne anye nọ akekpe ikpe abiide anọ ammọ. <verse eid="JDG 4:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JDG 4:6" />Anye amaadọñ ekekoot Barak ayịn Abinoam a-aketooho Kedes ke Naftali anyʌñ abo anye, “<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, Abasi Isrel, unọ fiin ewʌhọ ate, ‘Kaa, ben awo tọsịn duob (10,000) ke Naftali ye Sebulọn nyʌñ dat ammọ usʌñ dọọk kaa abod Tabọ. <verse eid="JDG 4:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JDG 4:7" />Ami ñyaadat Sisera, adaiso mbon ekọñ Yabịn, ye mme sariọd amọ ye mme udịmekọñ amọ ñkaa ke inyañ Kisọn ñnyʌñ ñyaak anye usịn fiin ke ubọk.’ ”<verse eid="JDG 4:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="JDG 4:8" />Barak amaabọọrọ anye ate, “Adieke afo asañake ye ami, ami ñyaakaa; ado adieke afo umuusañake ye ami, ami ndiikaaha.”<verse eid="JDG 4:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="JDG 4:9" />Debọra amaabo anye, “Ke akpanikọ ami ñyaukeene fiin ñkaa, ado afo uduukịtte unen ke ñkpọ ami, sia Abọọñ ayaayaak Sisera asịn awonwaan ke ubọk.” Ndin Debọra amaakeene Barak akaa Kedes. <verse eid="JDG 4:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JDG 4:10" />Ndin Barak amaakoot Sebulọn ye Naftali eka Kedes, ye awo tọsịn duob (10,000) ekedọọhọ eka ke idak amọ nte adaiwuod. Debọra amaanyʌñ akeene anye adọọk.<verse eid="JDG 4:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="JDG 4:11" />Ndin Heba awo Keen amaakpọñ mbon Keen mfen, ake ubon Hobab, ayịneka awodeen anwaan Moses,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4:11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Akeme ido ete anwaan Moses</char></note> anyʌñ akewuuk atayad amọ ke mben ekamba eto ke Saananịm a-akekpereke Kedes.<verse eid="JDG 4:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="JDG 4:12" />Ke ini ammọ ekedọkkọke Sisera ke Barak ayịn Abinoam amaadọọk akaa ke abod Tabọ, <verse eid="JDG 4:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JDG 4:13" />Sisera amaakoot afịd mme ideen ye sariọd ikie usʌkkeed ekedatta ukwak enam ato Harosed Hakoyịm ekaa inyañ Kisọn.<verse eid="JDG 4:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="JDG 4:14" />Akema Debọra amaabo Barak, “Kaa! Mfịn ado usen <char style="nd">A-Abọọñ</char> ayaaha Sisera usịn fiin ke ubọk. Nte <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ikubemme fiin iso ika?” Ndin Barak amaasọiyọ ke Abod Tabọ, ye ideen tọsịn duob (10,000) usʌkkeed ekekeeneke anye. <verse eid="JDG 4:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JDG 4:15" />Nte Barak akekaaha, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaasuan Sisera ye afịd sariọd ye mbon ekọñ amọ ke akañkañ, Sisera amaanyʌñ asọiyọ ke sariọd amọ afeghe ke ukod.<verse eid="JDG 4:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="JDG 4:16" />Barak amaabịne mme sariọd ye mbon ekọñ tutu akewuọ Harosed Hakoyịm, ndin afịd udịmekọñ Sisera emaeduọññọ ke iso akañkañ; awo ndomokeed ikisʌhọke. <verse eid="JDG 4:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JDG 4:17" />Ndin Sisera, amaafeghe ke ukod akaa atayad Yael, anwaan Heba awo Keen, sia ndukoppo amaaba ke ufọọd Yabịn adidem Hasọ ye ufọk Heba a-akedooho awo Keen.<verse eid="JDG 4:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="JDG 4:18" />Yael amaawuọ akaa akesoobo ye Sisera anyʌñ abo anye, “Di, abọọñ mmi, boiyo dʌk di. Kuufeghe ndịk.” Ndin anye amaadʌk atayad amọ, ndin anye amaafʌk anye ke afọñ atueb.<verse eid="JDG 4:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="JDG 4:19" />Anye amaabo, “Itọñ ansat miin, mbọk nnọ etok mmọọñ.” Anye amaatat ikpa mmọọñeba, anọ anye mmọọñ, anyʌñ afʌk anye.<verse eid="JDG 4:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="JDG 4:20" />Anye amaadọkkọ anye ate, “Da ke anyenusʌñ atayad. Adieke awo adiighe anyʌñ adu ubịp fiin, ‘Awo ndomokeed mmọaba do?’ bo ‘Iyoo.’ ”<verse eid="JDG 4:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="JDG 4:21" />Ado Yael, anwaan Heba, amaadat mboi atayad ye ukọññkpọ anyʌñ asọọp akaa ke ini anye akenaaha adaiya idab, ye akpọsọñ ekaha. Anye amaakọñ akọñ asịn anye ke awọñesịd tutu awʌhọ ke isọñ, ndin anye akpa.<verse eid="JDG 4:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="JDG 4:22" />Kpa idaha ado Barak amaadʌk adi ke itọk ubịne Sisera, Yael amaanyʌñ awuọ akesoobo ye anye. Anye amaabo, “Di, ami ñyauwọt fiin awo a-afo ayemme.” Ndin Barak amaakeene anye adʌk ufọk, ndin sese Sisera anaaha do ye mboi atayad ke ekoiso ammọ, amaakpa.<verse eid="JDG 4:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="JDG 4:23" />Ke usen ado Abasi amaasuuhọ Yabịn adidem Kenan anịm ke iso mbon Isrel. <verse eid="JDG 4:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JDG 4:24" />Ndin ubọk mbon Isrel amaanenekke afiik Yabịn adidem ke Kenan akpọsọñ-akpọsọñ tutu ammọ esobo anye.<verse eid="JDG 4:24" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JDG 4" />
  <chapter number="5" style="c" sid="JDG 5" />
  <para style="s1">Ikwọ Debọra</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JDG 5:1" />Ke usen ado Debọra ye Barak ayịn Abinoam emaekwọ ikwọ ami:<verse eid="JDG 5:1" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="JDG 5:2" />“Ke ini mme nditọ ideen mbọọñ ke Isrel edatta usʌñ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:2">ke ini mme awo ekemme esịd eyaak idem ammọ enọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:2">etooro <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>!<verse eid="JDG 5:2" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="JDG 5:3" />“Ikop ami, ndufo ndidem! Ikpañ utọñ, ndufo mme andikara!</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:3">Ami, kpa ami, ñyaakwọ nnọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:3">Ami ñyaatooro <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, kpa Abasi Isrel, ke ikwọ.<verse eid="JDG 5:3" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="JDG 5:4" />“Ke ini afo, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, akewuọhọ akpọñ Sei,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:4">ke ini afo akenamma isañ ato isọñ Edọm,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="JDG 5:4">isọñ amaanyeeñe, mme hefịn emaeduọk edịm,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:4">mme ikpaanyọñ emaeduọk mmọọñ.<verse eid="JDG 5:4" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="JDG 5:5" />Mme abod emaenyeeñe ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, kpa Abasi Sainai,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:5">ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, kpa Abasi Isrel.<verse eid="JDG 5:5" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="JDG 5:6" />“Ke ayio Samka ayịn Anad,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:6">ke ayio Yael, mme akpọusʌñ ekena ukpọk;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:6">mbon uka isañ ekesaña ke ñkwaña-ñkwaña usʌñ.<verse eid="JDG 5:6" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="JDG 5:7" />Mme ntək abio Isrel ikisinwanake anwan;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:7">ammọ emaemʌm enịm tutu ami, Debọra, ndakka nda,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:7">tutu ami ndakka nda, eka ke Isrel.<verse eid="JDG 5:7" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="JDG 5:8" />Abasi amaamek ufa mme adadusʌñ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:8">ke ini ekọñ akediighe inuaatob abio,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="JDG 5:8">ado awo ikikịtte atuekọñ mme eduad ndomokeed</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:8">ke atu tọsịn aba (40,000) ke Isrel.<verse eid="JDG 5:8" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="JDG 5:9" />Esịd mmi ada ye nditọ ideen mbọọñ Isrel,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:9">ye mbon e-enieghe esịd ñwaidem ke atu mbon awo.</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:9">Itooro <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>!<verse eid="JDG 5:9" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="JDG 5:10" />“Ndufo e-ewatta ke mme mfia dọñki,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:10">e-etieghe ke ndoppo afọñ esaña,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:10">ye ndufo e-esañake ke usʌñ,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="JDG 5:10">ikere ibaña <verse eid="JDG 5:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JDG 5:11" />uyio mme akwọikwọ ke mme itie uduọkmmọọñ.</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:11">Ammọ etañ mme edikan <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:11">mme edikan mbon idʌñ amọ ke Isrel.</para>
  <para style="b" vid="JDG 5:11" />
  <para style="q1" vid="JDG 5:11">“Akem mme ikọd <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char></para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:11">emaesuuk ekaa ke inuaatob abio.<verse eid="JDG 5:11" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="JDG 5:12" />‘Debọra, demme, demme!</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:12">Demme, demme, sio ikwọ</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="JDG 5:12">Dakka da, Barak!</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:12">Koono mbon amuumọ ke ekọñ, ayịn Abinoam.’<verse eid="JDG 5:12" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="JDG 5:13" />“Mme nsʌhọ mbọọñ abio emaesọiyọ edi;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:13">mme ikọd <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> emaesọiyọ edi eñkeene miin adinwana ye mbon uko.<verse eid="JDG 5:13" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="JDG 5:14" />Usʌk eketo Ifrem edi, a-ntịppe ammọ akedooho ke Amalek;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:14">Benyamin akeba ye mbon e-ekukeeneke fiin.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="JDG 5:14">Ke Makia mme adaukara emaesọiyọ edi,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:14">ke Sebulọn mbon e-ekamake esañ adaiwuod emaeda iso.<verse eid="JDG 5:14" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="JDG 5:15" />Mme nditọ ideen mbọọñ ke Isaka ekeba ye Debọra;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:15">ii, Isaka akeba ye Barak,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:15">ke ewʌhọ amọ emaedọñ ammọ eka ke itịkke.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="JDG 5:15">Ke mme abio ukara Rubịn</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:15">akpọsọñ uduuñọ esịd amaaba.<verse eid="JDG 5:15" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="JDG 5:16" />Ntak a-afo aketieghe ke mme abaedọñ-ọ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:16">adikop inuuk se mme udịmedọñ efịt-e?</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="JDG 5:16">Ke mme ñkañ ukara Rubịn</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:16">akpọsọñ uduuñọ esịd amaaba.<verse eid="JDG 5:16" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="JDG 5:17" />Kilied aketie ke edem Yọdan.</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:17">Ndin Daan, nsoo inam anye ateek ikpad ke mme nsʌñikañ?</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="JDG 5:17">Asaa atie ke mben esʌk</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:17">anyʌñ atie ke mben mbeghe ubom.<verse eid="JDG 5:17" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="JDG 5:18" />Mbon Sebulọn esịn kpa uwem ammọ ke ñkpañña;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:18">ukem ado ke Naftali akenam adika ke itịkke isọñ.<verse eid="JDG 5:18" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="JDG 5:19" />“Mme ndidem emaedi, ammọ emaenwana,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:19">mme ndidem Kenan emaenwana.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="JDG 5:19">Ke Taanak, ke mben mmọọñ Mekido,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:19">ammọ ikibenne mbịme silfa ndomokeed.<verse eid="JDG 5:19" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="JDG 5:20" />Ke anyọñ mme ntantaafiọñ emaenwana,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:20">ke mme usʌñ ammọ emaenwana ye Sisera.<verse eid="JDG 5:20" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="JDG 5:21" />Inyañ Kisọn amaakwọọk ammọ asio,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:21">akaan inyañ, kpa inyañ Kisọn.</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:21">Kaaka iso, ukpọñ mmi; sọñ idem!<verse eid="JDG 5:21" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="JDG 5:22" />Akem ñkpad enañmbakara emaesakka nte aduma,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:22">mme ñyaara enañmbakara amọ emaetamma ke uko ammọ. <verse eid="JDG 5:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JDG 5:23" />Enyere <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaabo, ‘Suuñọ Meros.’</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:23">‘Suuñọ mbon ammọ ataa idod-idod,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="JDG 5:23">sia ammọ ikidiighe idinwam <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:23">idinwam <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> adinwana ye mme ñkpọsọñ awo.’<verse eid="JDG 5:23" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="JDG 5:24" />“Anenekke afọn anọ Yael ke atu mme ibaan,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:24">anwaan Heba a-atooho Keen,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:24">anye e-ediọññọ ekan ke atu ibaan e-edʌñọke ke atayad.<verse eid="JDG 5:24" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="JDG 5:25" />Sisera akebeeñe mmọọñ, ado Yael amaanọ anye mmọọñeba;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:25">ke iko a-adotto mbọọñ anye amaasio mbad-mbad mmọọñeba anọ anye.<verse eid="JDG 5:25" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="JDG 5:26" />Anye amaanyan ubọk aben mboi atayad,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:26">ubọk nnasia amọ amaaben ukọññkpọ anamusọ.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="JDG 5:26">Anye amaakọñ Sisera, anuak anye iwuod</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:26">anye amaasuan anyʌñ atịppe anye akoiso.<verse eid="JDG 5:26" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="JDG 5:27" />Ke ukod amọ anye amaanʌhọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:27">anye amaaduọ; ke itie ado ke anye akenaa.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="JDG 5:27">Ke ukod amọ ke anye akenʌhọ, amaanyʌñ aduọ;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:27">itie a-anye akenʌhọke, ndo ke anye akeduọ, akenyʌñ akpa.<verse eid="JDG 5:27" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="JDG 5:28" />“Eka Sisera amaada ke ubenafịm anyuuñọ;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:28">ada ke edemusʌñ asio uyio atua ayịd,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="JDG 5:28">Ntak a-sariọd amọ akpeeneke adinyọñ ndi-e?</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:28">Ntak u-uyom ukod enañmbakara a-awatta sariọd amọ akpeeneke-e?<verse eid="JDG 5:28" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="JDG 5:29" />Mbon nti ifiọk ñkan ke atu mme ibaan amọ ebọọrọ anye;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:29">ke akpanikọ, anye aka iso adidọkkọ idem amọ,<verse eid="JDG 5:29" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="JDG 5:30" />‘Nte ammọ iyemme inyʌññọ ibaaña mme mbịme:</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:30">awonwaan keed me iba anie awodeen keed,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="JDG 5:30">mfọọn afọñ nte mbịme anọ Sisera,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:30">mfọọn afọñ se edọk yak ayaiya,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="JDG 5:30">ataa nti udọdọk afọñ ke itọñ mmi</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:30">afịd ami ado mbịme?’<verse eid="JDG 5:30" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="JDG 5:31" />“<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, yak afịd mme asua mfo etak!</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:31">Ado yak afịd mbon se uma fiin etie nte utịn</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 5:31">ke ini anye asakkake ke adudu amọ.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 5:31">Akema isọñ amaanie emem ke isua aba.<verse eid="JDG 5:31" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JDG 5" />
  <chapter number="6" style="c" sid="JDG 6" />
  <para style="s1">Kidiọn</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JDG 6:1" />Mbon Isrel emaenam idiọọkñkpọ ke iso Abọọñ, ndin ke isua itiaba anye amaaben ammọ asịn ke ubọk mbon Midian. <verse eid="JDG 6:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JDG 6:2" />Sia adudu Midian akesaña ye akpọsọñ ufiik, mbon Isrel emaenam itie idʌñ enọ idem ammọ ke abaitiad, ke ndudu ye ñkpọsọñ itie. <verse eid="JDG 6:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JDG 6:3" />Ini akeedodo a-mbon Isrel eketọọhọ mfịd ke inwañ, mbon Midian, Amalek ye mbon edem usakkautịn mfen emaeben ekọñ edʌk abio. <verse eid="JDG 6:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JDG 6:4" />Ammọ emaedʌñ ke isọñ enyʌñ ebiat mfịd inwañ ke afịd usʌñ tutu akesịm Kasa, ikiinyʌññọ isaana aduuwem ñkpọ ndomokeed ke Isrel iyaak, ye ke adooho edọñ me enañ me dọñki. <verse eid="JDG 6:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JDG 6:5" />Ammọ ekedi ye mme ufene ammọ ye mme atayad ammọ nte udịm ñkukuñkpọyọriyọ. Amaasọñ adibat ammọ ye mme kamel ammọ; ammọ ekedʌk isọñ edibabiat anye. <verse eid="JDG 6:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JDG 6:6" />Mbon Midian emaenam mbon Isrel eweene tutu ammọ eseeme enọ Abọọñ eyem unwam.<verse eid="JDG 6:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="JDG 6:7" />Ke ini mbon Isrel ekeseemeke enọ Abọọñ ke ntak mbon Midian, <verse eid="JDG 6:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JDG 6:8" />anye amaadọñ prọfed utom ate akedọkkọ ammọ, “Ami ado se Abọọñ, Abasi Isrel, atañ: Ami ñkisịññe ndufo ke Iyib, ke isọñ ufʌn ndọọk ndi. <verse eid="JDG 6:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JDG 6:9" />Ami ñkisịññe ndufo ke ubọk mbon Iyib, ñnyʌñ ifak ndufo nsịññe ke ubọk mbon se ikiifiik ndufo. Ami ñke abịne ammọ nsịññe ñnyʌñ mben isọñ ammọ inọ ndufo. <verse eid="JDG 6:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JDG 6:10" />Ndin ami mmaibo ndufo, ‘Ami ndo Abọọñ Abasi ndufo; ikiikpono abasi mbon Amọọ, a-ndufo edʌñọke ke isọñ ammọ.’ Ado ndufo ikiikpañña utọñ innọ miin.”<verse eid="JDG 6:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="JDG 6:11" />Enyere <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadi anyʌñ adiitie ke idak eto afriyo ke Ọfra a-akenieghe Yoas awo Abiesa, ke itie a-ayịn awodeen amọ Kidiọn akesatta wiid ke ukwak unam ukọd mbaak mbon Midian ekuudʌk. <verse eid="JDG 6:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JDG 6:12" />Ke ini enyere Abọọñ akebiọññọke anọ Kidiọn, anye amaabo, “Abọọñ a-aba ye afo, uko ke ekọñ.”<verse eid="JDG 6:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="JDG 6:13" />Kidiọn amaabọọrọ, “Feen nnọ miin, abọọñ mmi, ado adieke Abọọñ abaaha ye ñnyịn, ntak afịd mme ñkpọ ami atịppeke inọọ ñnyịn-e? Mmọ afịd mme utịppeñkpọ a-mme eteete ñnyịn eketañña inọọ ñnyịn ebaña ke ini ammọ ekebooho, ‘Nte idooho Abọọñ akiisio ñnyịn ke Iyib adi?’ Ado idahami Abọọñ amaisịn ñnyịn anyʌñ iyaak ñnyịn asịn ke ubọk Midian.”<verse eid="JDG 6:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="JDG 6:14" />
    <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaawọññọ ase anye anyʌñ abo, “Kaa ke ukeme a-afo anieghe nyʌñ nyaaña Isrel sio ke ubọk Midian. Nte idooho ami mbo yak aka?”<verse eid="JDG 6:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="JDG 6:15" />Kidiọn amaabọọrọ, “Feen nnọ miin, abọọñ mmi,” “ado mbo nnam die ñnyaaña Isrel? Ekpək mmi ado andinana inweek ñkan ke Manase, ndin ami ñnyʌñ ndo ataa usʌhọde etəkayịn ke ufọk ñnyịn.”<verse eid="JDG 6:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="JDG 6:16" />Ado Abọọñ amaabọọrọ Kidiọn, “Ami ñyaaba ye afo, ndin afo ayaawoot afịd mbon Midian, usʌhọke ndomokeed ke uwem.”<verse eid="JDG 6:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="JDG 6:17" />Kidiọn amaabọọrọ, “Adieke afo anenne iso ye ami idahami, nnọ miin idiọọñọ a-awọttọ abo ke ado afo atañ ikọ ye ami. <verse eid="JDG 6:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JDG 6:18" />Mbọk kuudakka unyọñ tutu ami ntịmme ndi ñnyʌñ mben uwa enọ mmi nduunịm fiin ke iso.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 6:18">
    <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaabo Kidiọn, “Ami ñyaabet tutu afo atịmme adi.”<verse eid="JDG 6:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="JDG 6:19" />Kidiọn amaadʌk ufọk, atem ñyịn ebod, ndin adat ndomuyo ke udomo efa keed anam uyo se yiis imiisịneke. Asịn unam ke akpasa anyʌñ adọñ mbad afere amọ ke ako, anye amaakoono ammọ awuọ adi anyʌñ adinọ anye ke idak eto afriyo.<verse eid="JDG 6:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="JDG 6:20" />Enyere Abasi amaabo anye, “Ben unam ado ye uyo se yiis imiisịneke, boon ammọ ke anyọñ itiad, nyʌñ nwañña mbad afere duọk.” Kidiọn amaanam ntoro. <verse eid="JDG 6:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JDG 6:21" />Akem enyere <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadat iwuod esañ amọ akesịneke anye ke ubọk atuuk unam ado ye uyo se yiis imiisịneke. Ikañ amaabịppe ke itiad, ata unam ado ye uyo. Ndin enyere Abọọñ amaasop. <verse eid="JDG 6:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JDG 6:22" />Ke ini Kidiọn akekịtte ke akedo enyere Abọọñ, anye amaasio ñkpo ate, “Sai, Abọọñ Andikara! Ami mmekịt enyere Abọọñ iso ye iso!”<verse eid="JDG 6:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="JDG 6:23" />Ado <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaabo anye, “Bọ emem! Kuufeghe ndịk. Afo uduukpaaha.”<verse eid="JDG 6:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="JDG 6:24" />Ndin Kidiọn amaabọp akpokoro uwa anọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke itie ado anyʌñ akoot anye itie ado, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ado Emem. Tutu mfịn ami anye mmọdo ke Ọfra ake mbon Abiesa.<verse eid="JDG 6:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="JDG 6:25" />Kpa ke akonayio ado Abọọñ amaabo anye, “Ben udiana ayaaraenañ ke atu udịmenañ ete mfo, anye a-adooho isua itiaba ke emana. Wuut akpokoro uwa Baal ete mfo nyʌñ kpịkke abai Asera adaaha akpere anye. <verse eid="JDG 6:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="JDG 6:26" />Ndin bọp ataa nnen-nnen akpokoro uwa nọ Abọọñ Abasi mfo ke anyọñ akpọsọñ abod ami. Dat eto abai Asera a-afo akekpịkkeke, dat udiana ayaaraenañ ado nam ufọfọb uwa.”<verse eid="JDG 6:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="JDG 6:27" />Ndin Kidiọn amaadat nditọufọk amọ duob anyʌñ anam se Abọọñ akedọkkọ anye. Ado sia anye akekoppo ndịk ke ntak ufọk amọ ye mbon abio, anye akenam adinam ami ke akonayio ke ini akpekedooho uweemeayio.<verse eid="JDG 6:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="JDG 6:28" />Ke usiere ubakusen ke ini mme awo ke abio ekedemmeke, emaewuut akpokoro uwa Baal, enyʌñ ekpịkke eto abai Asera a-akedaaha ke mben ado ye ayọhọ ayaaraenañ iba e-ekewaaha ke ufa akpokoro uwa e-ekebọppọ!<verse eid="JDG 6:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="JDG 6:29" />Ammọ emaebịp emọ-emọ ebo, “Anie akenam ñkpọ ami?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 6:29">Ke ini ammọ emaekenekke enam nduuñọ, emaedọkkọ ammọ ebo, “Kidiọn, ayịn Yoas akenam ñkpọ ado.”<verse eid="JDG 6:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="JDG 6:30" />Mbon abio ado emaebo Yoas, “Sio ayịn awodeen mfo di. Ana nte anye akpa, sia anye awuut akpokoro uwa Baal anyʌñ akpịkke eto abai Asera a-akedaaha ke ñkañ amọ.”<verse eid="JDG 6:30" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="JDG 6:31" />Ado Yoas amaabọọrọ atu mbon iyadesịd e-ekekannake anye ekʌk, “Nte ndufo eyem edinwana anwan nnọọ Baal? Nte ndufo enwana adinyaaña anye? Ana ewot awo akeedodo a-anwanake anọ anye ke ayio amaasiere! Adieke Baal ke akpanikọ adooho abasi, anye anie ukeme adinwana anwan idem amọ ke ini awo awuudo akpokoro uwa amọ.” <verse eid="JDG 6:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="JDG 6:32" />Ndin sia adooho Kidiọn akewuut akpokoro uwa Baal, ammọ emaenọ anye anyịñ Yerub-Baal ke usen ado, enyʌñ ebo, “Yak Baal anwana ye anye.”<verse eid="JDG 6:32" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="JDG 6:33" />Ndin afịd mbon Midian, Amalek ye mbon edem usakkautịn mfen emaediana keed ekaaña Yọdan eketie ke Abedeñ Yesriil. <verse eid="JDG 6:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="JDG 6:34" />Akema Sịbidịd Abọọñ amaadoro Kidiọn, ndin anye amaafịt adukpoñ, akoot mbon Abiesa ete ikeene imọ. <verse eid="JDG 6:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="JDG 6:35" />Anye amaadọñ mme isʌñutom edʌk afịd Manase, ekoot ammọ eben ñkpọ ekọñ, enyʌñ edʌk ke Asaa, Sebulọn ye Naftali, nọ ammọ ñko ewuọñọ edọọk ekesoobo ye ammọ.<verse eid="JDG 6:35" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="JDG 6:36" />Kidiọn amaabo Abasi, “Adieke adooho afo ayaanyaaña Isrel ato ke ubọk mmi naña afo akenwọñọ <verse eid="JDG 6:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="JDG 6:37" />se, ami ñyaabịt idededọñ ke afe ubeek abakpa. Adieke mbara abaaha ke ided ado ikpọọñ ado afịd isọñ ado nsaad, ndin ami ñyaadiọọñọ ke afo ayaanyaaña Isrel ato ubọk mmi, naña afo aketañ.” <verse eid="JDG 6:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="JDG 6:38" />Ndin kpa se ikiitịppe akedo ado. Kidiọn amaabak ademme ke usiere edem usen; ndin anye amaafʌt anyʌñ anyịmme mbara mmọọñ a-akeyọhọke iko asio.<verse eid="JDG 6:38" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" sid="JDG 6:39" />Akem Kidiọn amaabo Abasi, “Kuuyat esịd ye ami. Yak nnam ebeeñe keed mfen kpọd. Yak ami ndat idededọñ nnam idomo keed mfen, ado ini anye ami nam idededọñ asat ndin yak mbara afʌk isọñ.” <verse eid="JDG 6:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="JDG 6:40" />Ke akonayio ado Abasi amaanam ntoro. Idededọñ ikpọọñ akesat; mbara amaanyʌñ afʌk afịd isọñ.<verse eid="JDG 6:40" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JDG 6" />
  <chapter number="7" style="c" sid="JDG 7" />
  <para style="s1">Kidiọn Akan Mbon Midian</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JDG 7:1" />Ke ubak-ubak usen, Yerub-Baal (a-adooho Kidiọn) ye afịd mbon amọ emaebọp atayad ammọ ke ñkpere idịm Harọd. Itie nnaaekọñ mbon Midian akedo ke anyọñ-anyọñ ake ammọ ke itịkke a-akekpereke abod More. <verse eid="JDG 7:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JDG 7:2" /><char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaabo Kidiọn, “Ideen se afo anie ewak ebọhọ. Ami ñkemeke adiyaak Midian nsịn ammọ ke ubọk, imiidooho Isrel ayaanam inua ate, ‘Ukeme mmi amaañnyaaña miin.’ <verse eid="JDG 7:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JDG 7:3" />Idahami dọkkọ mbon ekọñ. ‘Awo keed akeedodo a-akoppo ndịk akeme adiwọññọ iso ñnyọñ ñkpọñ abod Kilied.’ ” Akem awo tọsịn edịb mme iba (22,000) emaenyọñọ, ke ini tọsịn duob (10,000) ekesʌhọke.<verse eid="JDG 7:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="JDG 7:4" />Ado <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaabo Kidiọn, “Ideen esʌk ewawak. Ben ammọ sọiyọ kaa mmọọñ, ndin ami ñyaasara ammọ nsio nnam nọ asịb unọ fiin ke itie ado. Adieke ami mbooho, ‘Anye ami ayaakaa ye afo,’ anye ayaakaa; ado adieke ami mbooho, ‘Anye ami idiikaaha ye afo,’ anye idiikaaha.”<verse eid="JDG 7:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="JDG 7:5" />Ndin Kidiọn amaaben mbon ado akaa ke mmọọñ. Do Abọọñ amaadọkkọ anye abo, “Bakka mbon se idadai mmọọñ ke edeme ammọ nte ewa adai sio kpọñ atu mbon etọọñọketọọñọ edọñ enwọñ.” <verse eid="JDG 7:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JDG 7:6" />Ikie ita (300) ke atu ammọ ekekama ubọk nte kọọb enwọñ, edai nte ewa. Afịd mbon ako emaesuuk esọrọ ke edọñ ammọ enwọñ mmọọñ.<verse eid="JDG 7:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="JDG 7:7" />
    <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaabo Kidiọn, “Ñyaadat awo ikie ita (300) ekedaiyadai mmọọñ unyaaña fiin ñnyʌñ ñyaak mbon Midian usịn fiin ke ubọk. Yak afịd mbon ako enyọñọ ufọk.” <verse eid="JDG 7:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JDG 7:8" />Ndin Kidiọn amaanam mbon Isrel se ikisʌhọ enyọñọ ufọk ado anye amaanịm ikie ita (300), e-ekekoonoke ndidia ye mme adukpoñ mbon ako.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 7:8">Ndin itie nnaaekọñ Midian akeda akpere anye ke abedeñ. <verse eid="JDG 7:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JDG 7:9" />Ke akonayio ado Abọọñ amaabo Kidiọn, “Dakka da, sọiyọ kaa itie nnaaekọñ, sia ami ñyaayaak anye usịn fiin ke ubọk. <verse eid="JDG 7:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JDG 7:10" />Adieke afo afegheke ndịk aditop ekọñ, sọiyọ kaa do ye ayịnufọk mfo Pura <verse eid="JDG 7:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JDG 7:11" />nyʌñ kpañ utọñ kop se ammọ etañ. Ado amaaboiyo, afo ayaanie nsọọñọnda adinwana ekọñ ke itie nnaaekọñ.” Ndin anye ye Pura ayịnufọk amọ emaesọiyọ ekaa ñkpere itie nnaaekọñ. <verse eid="JDG 7:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JDG 7:12" />Mbon Midian, mbon Amalek ye afịd mbon edem usakkautịn emaedʌñ ke itịkke, ewak nte ñkukuñkpọyọriyọ. Nte ntan ke mben akpainyañ, awo ikiikanna adibat mme kamel ammọ.<verse eid="JDG 7:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="JDG 7:13" />Kidiọn amaadiwuọ itie ado kpa ke idaha e-ete keed akesʌkkọ adọkkọ ufan amọ ndab amọ. Anye amaabo ate “Ami mmaadappa ndab. Ikara-ikara efiak uyo e-ekamake baali enam amaawere adʌk itie nnaaekọñ mbon Midian. Anye amaatọ atayad ke ataa akpọsọñ adudu a-akenamma atayad akappa akʌbọ anyʌñ awuudo.”<verse eid="JDG 7:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="JDG 7:14" />Ufan amọ amaabọọrọ abo, “Anye ami idooho ñkpọ mfen ikan akañkañ Kidiọn ayịn Yoas, awo Isrel. Abasi ayaak mbon Midian ye afịd itie nnaaekọñ ammọ asịn anye ke ubọk.”<verse eid="JDG 7:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="JDG 7:15" />Ke ini Kidiọn amaakekop ndab ami ye naña ekappa anye, anye amaatuak iwuod anyʌñ anọ Abasi ukpono. Ndin anye amaatịmme akaa ke itie nnaaekọñ Isrel anyʌñ akebọñ, “Idaaña ida! Abọọñ ayaak itie nnaaekọñ mbon Midian isịn ndufo ke ubọk.” <verse eid="JDG 7:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JDG 7:16" />Anye amaabakka awo ikie ita (300) ado adọñ ke ikpeghe mme itie ñka ita, ndin anye amaasịn mme adukpoñ ye ukpọk abañ ke ubọk afịd ammọ, ye mme utuenikañ ke esịd.<verse eid="JDG 7:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="JDG 7:17" />Anye amaabo ammọ, “Inse miin. Ikeene ndadusʌñ mmi. Ami mmaawuọ iwuod itie nnaaekọñ, inam ukem-ukem se ami nnam. <verse eid="JDG 7:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JDG 7:18" />Ke ini ami ye afịd mbon e-ebaaha ye ami ifịtte mme adukpoñ ñnyịn, ke afịd ñkanñkʌk itie nnaaekọñ ifịt ake ndufo inyʌñ ibọñ ñkpo, ‘Anie Abọọñ ye Kidiọn.’ ”<verse eid="JDG 7:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="JDG 7:19" />Kidiọn ye mme awo ikie ekesañake ye anye emaewuọ iwuod itie nnaaekọñ ke ntọọñọ ufọọd akonayio, kpa ke idaha a-ammọ ekepəhoke mbon ukpeme. Ammọ emaefịt mme adukpoñ ammọ enyʌñ eboom mme abañ a-ammọ ekekamake ke ubọk. <verse eid="JDG 7:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JDG 7:20" />Mme ikpeghe itie utom ita ado emaefịt adukpoñ enyʌñ eboom mme abañ. Ammọ emaesio ñkpo nte ammọ ekamake utuenikañ ke ubọk ufiin ye mme adukpoñ ammọ ke ubọk nnasia ete, “Akañkañ Abọọñ ye ake Kidiọn!” <verse eid="JDG 7:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JDG 7:21" />Ke ini awo keedekeed akedaaha ke itie amọ ekanna itie nnaaekọñ ekʌk, afịd mbon Midian emaekịppe itọk, enyʌñ ebọọñ ñkpo naña ammọ efeeñeke.<verse eid="JDG 7:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="JDG 7:22" />Ke ini adukpoñ ikie ita (300) akesioho uyio, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaanam mme awo ke afịd itie nnaaekọñ ewọññọ enwana ye emọ-emọ ke ikwa. Mbon ekọñ emaefeeñe tutu Bed Sita enen iso ese Serera tutu ke adaña Ebeel Mehola a-akpereke Tabad. <verse eid="JDG 7:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JDG 7:23" />Emaekoot mbon Isrel ke Naftali, ekoot mbon Asaa ye afịd mbon Manase ndin ammọ emaebịne mbon Midian. <verse eid="JDG 7:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JDG 7:24" />Akema Kidiọn amaadọñ mme isʌñutom eka ke afịd mme abod-abod abio ke Ifrem, anyʌñ abo ate, “Isọiyọ idiinwana ye mbon Midian inyʌñ iben mme mmọọñ Yọdan mbemiso ammọ edisịm tutu awuọ ke Bed Bara.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 7:24">Ndin emaekoot afịd ideen ke Ifrem esịññe edi ndin ammọ emaebiọñọ mme mmọọñ Yọdan tutu esịm Bed Bara. <verse eid="JDG 7:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JDG 7:25" />Ammọ emaenyʌñ emʌm mme adadusʌñ mbon Midian iba, Ọreb ye Siib. Emaenyʌñ ewot Ọreb ke itiad Ọreb, ndin Seeb ke itie unam ukọd Seeb. Ammọ emaebịne mbon Midian enyʌñ edat iwuod Ọreb ye ake Seeb esọk Kidiọn, a-akedaaha ke mben Yọdan.<verse eid="JDG 7:25" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JDG 7" />
  <chapter number="8" style="c" sid="JDG 8" />
  <para style="s1">Seba ye Salmuna</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JDG 8:1" />Ndin mbon Ifrem emaebịp Kidiọn, “Ntak a-afo anamma ntom ye ñnyịn-e? Nsoo ido nọ afo uduukukoodo ñnyịn ke ini afo akekaaha ekọñ ye Midian?” Ndin ammọ emaetañ ikọ ñnyanubọk ye anye adudu-adudu.<verse eid="JDG 8:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="JDG 8:2" />Ado anye amaabọọrọ ammọ ate, “Nsoo ke ami nnie ekemekke ediben ndomo ye ndufo? Nte aditañ kreb ke Ifrem ifọnnọ ikan ayọhọ idọk kreb Abiesa? <verse eid="JDG 8:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JDG 8:3" />Abasi amaaben Ọreb ye Seeb, mme adaiwuod Midian, isịn ndufo ke ubọk. Nsoo ke ami ñkekan adinam e-ekpedatta edomo ye ndufo?” Ke ami, iyadesịd ammọ ye anye amaasuuhọ.<verse eid="JDG 8:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="JDG 8:4" />Kidiọn ye ideen amọ awo ikie ita (300) ami, i-inweek amaakekweeñe emaeka iso ebịne ediwuọ Yọdan enyʌñ eboiyo anye. <verse eid="JDG 8:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JDG 8:5" />Anye amaabo mbon Sukọd ate, “Inọ udịmekọñ mmi uyo, sia idem amem ammọ, ndin ami nsʌk mbebịne Seba ye Salmuna, mme ndidem Midian.”<verse eid="JDG 8:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="JDG 8:6" />Ado mme adaaha ke Sukọd emaebo anye, “Nte afo amemọmʌm Seba ye Salmuna kaña? Ntak añnyịn ikpinọọhọ mme udịmekọñ mfo uyo-o?”<verse eid="JDG 8:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="JDG 8:7" />Akem Kidiọn amaabọọrọ, “Sia adooho ntoro, Abọọñ amaayaak Seba ye Salmuna ansịn miin ke ubọk, ami ñyaawai abʌkidem ndufo ke ñkukịm ye mbaraekpe akpautatan.”<verse eid="JDG 8:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="JDG 8:8" />Anye amaato do adakka akaa Peniel anyʌñ akenam ukem ebeeñe ado, ado mbon ado emaebọọrọ kpa naña mbon Sukọd ekebọọrọ. <verse eid="JDG 8:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JDG 8:9" />Ndin anye amaabọọrọ mbon Peniel abo, “Ami mmaakan ntịme ñnyọñ ndi, ñyaawuut tọwa ami.”<verse eid="JDG 8:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="JDG 8:10" />Idaha ado Seba ye Salmuna mmọdo ekeba ke Kakọ ye mbon ekọñ ekewakka ñkpọ nte awo tọsịn duob mme ition (15,000), afịd se ikisʌhọ ke atu mbon ekọñ ake edem usakkautịn; mbon ukama akañkañ tọsịn ikie keed mme edịb (120,000) emaeduọññọ. <verse eid="JDG 8:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JDG 8:11" />Kidiọn amaadakka adọọk ke usʌñ mbon ukpeme enañ ke edem usakkautịn Noba ye Yokbeha anyʌñ akenwana ekọñ ye mbon ekọñ i-imiikinieghe idodanyen. <verse eid="JDG 8:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JDG 8:12" />Seba ye Salmuna, mme ndidem Midian iba ado, emaefeeñe, ado anye amaabịne ammọ anyʌñ amuum ammọ, asuan afịd mbon ekọñ ammọ.<verse eid="JDG 8:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="JDG 8:13" />Akem Kidiọn ayịn Yoas amaasaña usʌñ a-aboiyoke Paas Heres anyọñ ekọñ. <verse eid="JDG 8:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JDG 8:14" />Anye amaamʌm akparawa keed ke Sukọd anyʌñ abịp anye mbuume, ndin akparawa ado amaawet anyịñ mme adaaha ata mme duob mme itiaba ekedooho mme ñkpisọñ ke Sukọd anọ anye. <verse eid="JDG 8:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JDG 8:15" />Akem Kidiọn amaadi anyʌñ adibo mbon Sukọd, “Se Seba ye Salmuna, a-ndufo ekennọọhọ ñnyọọ ebo, ‘Nte afo amemọmʌm Seba ye Salmuna kaña? Ntak añnyịn ikpinọọhọ udịmekọñ mfo e-ekoppo mmemidem uyo-o?’ ” <verse eid="JDG 8:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JDG 8:16" />Anye amaaben mme ñkpisọñ abio ado anọ ideen Sukọd ukpeebñkpọ ke adimia ammọ ufen ke ñkukịm ye mbaraekpe akpautatan. <verse eid="JDG 8:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JDG 8:17" />Anye ñko amaanyʌñ awuut tọwa ke Peniel anyʌñ awot mbon abio ado.<verse eid="JDG 8:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="JDG 8:18" />Akem anye amaabịp Seba ye Salmuna, “Nsoo utọ ideen ke ndufo ekewot ke Tabọ?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 8:18">Ammọ emaebọọrọ ete, “Ideen nte afo, ammọ keedekeed ekeba nte nditọ ideen mbọọñ.”<verse eid="JDG 8:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="JDG 8:19" />Kidiọn amaabọọrọ, “Ammọ ekedo nditọeka mmi, mme nditọ ideen eka mmi. Kpa nte Abọọñ aduuho uwem, adieke ndufo ekpekesaanake uwem ammọ eyaak, ami ñkpiwotto ndufo.” <verse eid="JDG 8:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JDG 8:20" />Ke adikanna iso nse Yeta, akpan amọ, anye amaabo, “Wot ammọ!” Ado Yeta ikiidʌttọ akañkañ amọ isio, sia anye akedo etəkayịn, ndịk amaanyʌñ amʌm anye.<verse eid="JDG 8:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="JDG 8:21" />Seba ye Salmuna emaebo anye, “Di, nam ke idem mfo. ‘Naña awo aba, kpa ntoro ke adudu amọ aba.’ ” Ndin Kidiọn amaawuọ adi anyʌñ awoot ammọ, anyʌñ akọññọ mme ñkpọ mbanaidem ke itọñ kamel ammọ.<verse eid="JDG 8:21" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Afọñ Aboditọñ Kidiọn</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="JDG 8:22" />Mbon Isrel emaebo Kidiọn, “Ikara ñnyịn: afo, ayịn awodeen mfo ye ayeyịn awodeen mfo sia afo amainyaaña ñnyịn asio ke ubọk mbon Midian.”<verse eid="JDG 8:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="JDG 8:23" />Ado Kidiọn amaabọọrọ ammọ abo, “Ami ndiikarake ndufo, ayịn mmi idiinyʌññọ ikara ndufo. Abọọñ adiikara ndufo.” <verse eid="JDG 8:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JDG 8:24" />Ndin Kidiọn amaabo, “Ami mmenie ebeeñe keed, yak ndufo keedekeed ennọ miin ñkpahautọñ ke atu udeeme mbịme ndufo.” (Akedo ido mbon Ismeel adisịne ñkpahautọñ kold.)<verse eid="JDG 8:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="JDG 8:25" />Ammọ emaebọọrọ ete, “Ñnyịn iyainọ ammọ ke inemesịd.” Ndin ammọ emaebịt afọñ, ammọ keedekeed enyʌñ etop ñkpannuun kold ke atu mbịme amọ edoot. <verse eid="JDG 8:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="JDG 8:26" />Udob ñkpannuun kold a-anye akebeeñeke amaasịm sekel ikie efịd aba (1,700). Awo ikibatta ñkpọ mbanaidem, ukọkọñọ ñkpọ ye iduod-iduod adisịne ñkpọ a-mme ndidem Midian ekesịneke ye mme ñkpọitọñ ekesikọọñọ mme kamel ammọ ke itọñ. <verse eid="JDG 8:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="JDG 8:27" />Kidiọn amaadat mme kold ami anam afọñ aboditọñ, a-anye akenịmme ke Ọfra, abio amọ. Afịd Isrel emaenam akpara ke adikpono ñkpọ ado, ndin anye amaanyʌñ akappa ado afia anọ Kidiọn ye ufọk amọ.<verse eid="JDG 8:27" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ñkpa Kidiọn</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="JDG 8:28" />Ntom ke ekenam Midian asuuk iwuod anọ mbon Isrel inyʌññọ idịppe iwuod aba. Ke ayio uwem Kidiọn, isọñ amaanie emem isua aba.<verse eid="JDG 8:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="JDG 8:29" />Yerub-Baal ayịn Yoas amaanyọñ idʌñ amọ akedʌñ. <verse eid="JDG 8:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="JDG 8:30" />Kidiọn ke idem amọ akenie nditọ ideen ata mme duob, sia anye amaadọ uwak ibaan. <verse eid="JDG 8:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="JDG 8:31" />Anwaan esa amọ, a-akedʌññọ ke Sekem, amaanyʌñ aman ayịn awodeen anọ anye, ndin anye amaasio ayịn ado Abimelek. <verse eid="JDG 8:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="JDG 8:32" />Kidiọn ayịn Yoas amaakpa ke ataa eti isua usọñ enyʌñ ebuuk anye ke udi ete amọ Yoas ke Ọfra ake Abiesa.<verse eid="JDG 8:32" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="JDG 8:33" />I-ikpeeneke Kidiọn akekpa ndin mbon Isrel emaetịmme esaña akpara ke adinam ñkpọ nnọọ Baal. Ammọ emaewuuk Baal-Berịd nte abasi ammọ, <verse eid="JDG 8:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="JDG 8:34" />ndin nditọ Isrel ikiitoiyoke Abọọñ Abasi ammọ, a-akesioho ammọ ke ubọk afịd mme asua ammọ ke afịd usʌñ. <verse eid="JDG 8:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="JDG 8:35" />Nditọ Isrel ñko emaetre edisuuk iwuod nnọọ ufọk Yerub-Baal (a-adooho Kidiọn) akpesʌkado nte anye akewaaha idem anam mme nti ñkpọ anọ ammọ.<verse eid="JDG 8:35" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JDG 8" />
  <chapter number="9" style="c" sid="JDG 9" />
  <para style="s1">Abimelek</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JDG 9:1" />Abimelek ayịn Yerub-Baal amaadakka akaa abịne nditọeka eka amọ ke Sekem anyʌñ akebo ammọ ye afịd ubon eka amọ ate, <verse eid="JDG 9:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JDG 9:2" />“Ibịp afịd mme amanaisọñ Sekem, ‘Anye akee ifọn ikan ye ndufo: adiyak afịd nditọ ideen Yerub-Baal ata mme duob ikara ndufo, me awo keed adikara?’ Itoiyo ke ami ndo abʌk ye iyiib ndufo.”<verse eid="JDG 9:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="JDG 9:3" />Ke ini nditọeka amọ ideen eketañña afịd ami enọ mme amanaisọñ Sekem, ammọ emaenyịmme edikeene Abimelek, sia ammọ ekebo, “Anye awuana ñkpọ ye ñnyịn.” <verse eid="JDG 9:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JDG 9:4" />Ammọ emaenọ anye sekel silfa ata mme duob (70) e-ekedatta eto tembịd Baal-Berịd, ndin Abimelek amaadat ami akpe mbon ntịme ye mbon mbubịk, e-ekekappake edo mme nsaña amọ. <verse eid="JDG 9:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JDG 9:5" />Anye amaakaa ufọk ete amọ ke Ọfra ndin ke anyọñ itiad keed anye amaawot afịd nditọete amọ awo ata mme duob, nditọ Yerub-Baal. Ado Yọtam, akpatre ayịn Yerub-Baal, amaabọkkọ afeghe akedịbe. <verse eid="JDG 9:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JDG 9:6" />Akem afịd mme amanaisọñ Sekem ye Bed Milo emaebono ke idak ekamba eto ke adaaha Sekem adinam Abimelek adidem.<verse eid="JDG 9:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="JDG 9:7" />Ke ini ekedọkkọke Yọtam ebaña ñkpọ ami, anye amaadọọk aka ke iwuod Abod Kerisịm akebọñ ñkpo akoot ammọ abo, “Ikpañ utọñ innọ miin, mme amanaisọñ Sekem, mbaak Abasi ñko akpañ utọñ inọ ndufo. <verse eid="JDG 9:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JDG 9:8" />Usen keed mme eto emaewuọ ekaa adiyet abọọñ adan nnọọ idem ammọ. Ammọ emaebo eto ọlif, ‘Do adidem ñnyịn.’<verse eid="JDG 9:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="JDG 9:9" />“Ado eto ọlif amaabọọrọ, ‘Nte a-afọn ami adikpọñ adan mmi, e-edatta ekpono mme abasi ye mme awo ñke kaara ke atu mme eto?’<verse eid="JDG 9:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="JDG 9:10" />“Mfen, mme eto emaebo eto fik, ‘Di do adidem ñnyịn.’<verse eid="JDG 9:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="JDG 9:11" />“Ado eto fik amaabọọrọ, ‘Nte a-afọn ami adikpọñ mfịd mmi, a-afọnnọ anyʌñ anem eti-eti, ndida ukara nnọ mme eto?’<verse eid="JDG 9:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="JDG 9:12" />“Akem mme eto emaebo fain, ‘Di do adidem ñnyịn.’<verse eid="JDG 9:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="JDG 9:13" />“Ado eto fain amaabọọrọ, ‘Nte a-afọn ami adikpọñ ukọd mmi, a-anọọhọ mme abasi ye mme awo inemesịd, ñke kaara ke atu mme eto?’<verse eid="JDG 9:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="JDG 9:14" />“Ke akpatre afịd mme eto emaebo mbaraekpe, ‘Di nyʌñ do adidem ñnyịn.’<verse eid="JDG 9:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="JDG 9:15" />“Mbaraekpe amaabo mme eto, ‘Adieke ke akpanikọ ndufo enekkeke eyem ediñyet miin adan nte adidem ndufo, idi inyʌñ idi idịbe ke idak mfuud mmi; ado adieke imiimaaha, yak ikañ awuọ ke mbaraekpe anyʌñ ata mme eto sida ke Lebanọn!’<verse eid="JDG 9:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="JDG 9:16" />“Nte ndufo emenam ami ke ido ukpono ye ke akpanikọ ke edinam Abimelek adidem? Nte ndufo emenam yak anen ye Yerub-Baal ye ufọk amọ? Nte ndufo emenam naña akpedot nọ enam ye anye? <verse eid="JDG 9:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JDG 9:17" />Itoiyo ke ete mmi akenwana ekọñ inọọ ndufo anyʌñ aduọọk uwem amọ mbaak inyaaña ndufo asio ke ubọk Midian. <verse eid="JDG 9:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JDG 9:18" />Ado mfịn ami ndufo emedakka eda enwana ye ufọk ete mmi. Ndufo emaewot nditọ amọ ata mme duob ke anyọñ itiad keed e-enyʌñ enam Abimelek, ayịn ifʌn awonwaan amọ ado adidem anọ mme amanaisọñ Sekem sia anye awuana ñkpọ ye ndufo. <verse eid="JDG 9:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JDG 9:19" />Nte ndufo ekenam ami ke ido ukpono ye ke akpanikọ enọ Yerub-Baal ye ufọk amọ? Adieke akedoho ntoro, yak Abimelek ado idaara ndufo, ndufo ñko enyʌñ edo idaara amọ! <verse eid="JDG 9:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JDG 9:20" />Ado adieke ndufo imiikinamma ado, yak ikañ awuọ ke Abimelek ita ndufo, mbọọñ ye mme amanaisọñ Sekem ye Bed Milo, yak ikañ anyʌñ awuọ ke ndufo, mme amanaisọñ Sekem ye Bed Milo, ata Abimelek.”<verse eid="JDG 9:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="JDG 9:21" />Akem Yọtam amaafeghe akaa Bee akedʌñ ke udo sia anye amaakop ndịk abaña ayịnete amọ Abimelek.<verse eid="JDG 9:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="JDG 9:22" />Ke Abimelek amaakekara Isrel isua ita, <verse eid="JDG 9:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JDG 9:23" />Abasi amaasịn usua ke ufọọd Abimelek ye mme amanaisọñ Sekem ndin ammọ emaenam abiaña ye Abimelek. <verse eid="JDG 9:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JDG 9:24" />Abasi akenam ami nọ ato do aben idiọọk e-ekenamma nditọ Yerub-Baal ata mme duob (70) ke adiduọk iyiib ammọ, asio ayịneka ammọ Abimelek usiene ye mme amanaisọñ Sekem e-ekenwamma anye adiwoot nditọete amọ. <verse eid="JDG 9:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JDG 9:25" />Ke ediwọt nsọñiwuod ye anye, mme amanaisọñ ideen Sekem emaesịn mme awo ke iwuod abod ke ikọd enyʌñ emuum mme awo emaana eyiip ñkpọ mbon awo se ikisaña ke usʌñ ado, ndin emaeben ami eketañ enọ Abimelek.<verse eid="JDG 9:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="JDG 9:26" />Ndin Kaal, ayịn awodeen Ebed, amaakaa akedʌñ ke Sekem ye ekpək amọ, ndin mme amanaisọñ ado emaenie mbuọdidem ke idem amọ. <verse eid="JDG 9:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="JDG 9:27" />Ke ammọ emaekewuọ eka inwañ fain enyʌñ ebok mme mfịd kreb, efiik ammọ, ammọ emaenam usọrọ ke tembịd abasi ammọ. Ke ini ammọ ekesʌkkọ edia enyʌñ enwọñ ñkpọ, ammọ emaesuuñọ Abimelek. <verse eid="JDG 9:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="JDG 9:28" />Akem Kaal ayịn Ebed amaabo, “Anie awo ado Abimelek, ntak añnyịn mbon Sekem ikpi isịneke ke idak amọ-ọ? Idooho anye ado ayịn Yerub-Baal, ndin idooho Sebuul ado udiana amọ? Inam ñkpọ inọ ufọk Hamọọ, ete Sekem! Ntak añnyịn ikpi inamma ñkpọ inọọ Abimelek-e? <verse eid="JDG 9:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="JDG 9:29" />Ubaha akpedooho ibon ami ekesịne ke idak ewʌhọ mmi! Ndin ami ñkpaadooro anye nsio. Ñkpaabo Abimelek, ‘Koot afịd mbon ekọñ mfo ewuọ edi!’ ”<verse eid="JDG 9:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="JDG 9:30" />Ke ini Sebuul adaiwuod ukara abio ado akekoppo se Kaal ayịn Ebed aketañ, anye amaayat esịd eti-eti. <verse eid="JDG 9:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="JDG 9:31" />Anye amaadọñ mme isʌñutom anọ Abimelek ke ndịbe, abo “Kaal ayịn Ebed ye ekpək amọ emaedi ke Sekem enyʌñ etịmede abio ubaña fiin. <verse eid="JDG 9:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="JDG 9:32" />Ndin idahami, ama ado ke akonayio afo ye mbon mfo enie ediwuọ ñkedịbe ke ikọd. <verse eid="JDG 9:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="JDG 9:33" />Ke ndañ nsiere ke usakkautịn, idọọk abio inam ekọñ. Kaal ye mbon amọ emaewuọñọ edi ekọñ ye afo, dat ufañ ado wot ammọ.”<verse eid="JDG 9:33" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="JDG 9:34" />Ndin Abimelek ye afịd udịmekọñ amọ emaewuọ ke akonayio enyʌñ ekedịbe itie a-akpereke Sekem ke ikpeghe inaañ. <verse eid="JDG 9:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="JDG 9:35" />Idaha ntoro Kaal ayịn Ebed amaawuọ akeda ke inua atob abio kpa ke ini Abimelek ye udịmekọñ amọ ekewuọñọke ke itie udịbe ammọ.<verse eid="JDG 9:35" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="JDG 9:36" />Ke ini Kaal akekịtte ammọ, anye amaabo Sebuul, “Se, mme awo esʌk esọiyọ ke mme abod edi!”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 9:36">Sebuul amaanyʌñ abọọrọ, “Afo anam ndudue ke adikịt ndukpọñ abod nte mme awo.”<verse eid="JDG 9:36" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" sid="JDG 9:37" />Ado Kaal amaamaana abenne uyio abo, “Se, mme awo esʌk esọiyọ edi ke ufọọd etəkabod, ikpeghe keed asʌk ato adi ke ñkañ eto mbon useñkpọ.”<verse eid="JDG 9:37" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" sid="JDG 9:38" />Ndin Sebuul amaabo anye, “Mmọ anye ñkpooninua mfo idahami, afo a-akebooho, ‘Anie ido Abimelek a-anaaha ñnyịn isịne ke idak amọ inam ñkpọ inọ anye?’ Nte idooho ideen ami ke afo akesak nsaha? Wuọ kaa ke nwana ye ammọ!”<verse eid="JDG 9:38" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" sid="JDG 9:39" />Ndin Kaal adaiwuod amaaben mme amanaisọñ Sekem anyʌñ akenwana ye Abimelek. <verse eid="JDG 9:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="JDG 9:40" />Abimelek amaadubịnne anye ke afịd usʌñ tutu akesịm inuaatob, emaenyʌñ ewoot uwak awo naña ammọ efeeñeke. <verse eid="JDG 9:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="JDG 9:41" />Akem Abimelek amaadʌñ ke Aruma, ndin Sebuul amaabịne Kaal ye ekpək amọ asio ke Sekem.<verse eid="JDG 9:41" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" sid="JDG 9:42" />Edemusen, mbon Sekem emaewuọñọ ekaa inwañ, ndin emaeben ekebʌk enọ Abimelek. <verse eid="JDG 9:42" /><verse number="43" style="v" sid="JDG 9:43" />Ndin anye amaaben mbon amọ, abakka ammọ asịn ke ikpeghe ita anyʌñ anam ammọ edịbe ke ikọd ebet. Ke ini anye akekịtte ammọ nte ewuọñọ ke abio edi, anye amaadakka ada anwana ye ammọ. <verse eid="JDG 9:43" /><verse number="44" style="v" sid="JDG 9:44" />Abimelek ye mme ikpeghe ekọñ e-ekebaaha ye anye emaesọsọp ewuọ ekedat itie ke inuaatob abio. Ndin ikpeghe iba emaenwana ye mbon e-ekebaaha ke inwañ enyʌñ ewoot ammọ. <verse eid="JDG 9:44" /><verse number="45" style="v" sid="JDG 9:45" />Afịd usen ado Abimelek amaasọọñọ afiik anwan ke abio ado tutu adat anye anyʌñ awoot mme awo ke esịd. Ndin anye amaasobo abio ado anyʌñ asuan inʌñ ke esịd.<verse eid="JDG 9:45" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="46" style="v" sid="JDG 9:46" />Ke ini ekekoppo ami, mme amanaisọñ e-ekebaaha ke tọwa Sekem emaewuọñọ ekaa akpọsọñ itie ke tembịd El-Berid. <verse eid="JDG 9:46" /><verse number="47" style="v" sid="JDG 9:47" />Ke ini Abimelek akekoppo ke mme mbọọñ Tọwa Sekem emaekeboho do, <verse eid="JDG 9:47" /><verse number="48" style="v" sid="JDG 9:48" />Abimelek ye afịd ideen amọ emaedakka edọọk ekaa ke Abod Salmọn. Anye amaadat ekịd anyʌñ akpịkke usʌk ñkọk eto, anyʌñ adịppe adoot ke afara amọ. Ndin anye amaanọ ideen amọ uyio ate, “Isọsọp! Inam se ndufo ekịt naña ami nnam!” <verse eid="JDG 9:48" /><verse number="49" style="v" sid="JDG 9:49" />Ndin afịd mme awo emaekpịkke ñkọk eto enyʌñ ekeene Abimelek. Ammọ emaebok anye ke akpọsọñ itie enyʌñ esịn ikañ ke ini mme awo esʌkkọ edọñọ ke esịd. Ndin afịd mme awo ke tọwa Sekem, ñkpọ nte awo tọsịn keed ideen ye ibaan, emaekpañña ekọrọ.<verse eid="JDG 9:49" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="50" style="v" sid="JDG 9:50" />Ñko Abimelek amaakaa Tebes akesuakka anye anyʌñ aben anye adat. <verse eid="JDG 9:50" /><verse number="51" style="v" sid="JDG 9:51" />Ke esịd abio, asọñ idem tọwa amaaba, a-afịd ideen ye ibaan, afịd mme amanaisọñ abio ado ekefeeñeke ekedọñọ. Ammọ emaeyịt usʌñ esịn idem ammọ ke esịd enyʌñ edọọk ekaa ke akọm tọwa. <verse eid="JDG 9:51" /><verse number="52" style="v" sid="JDG 9:52" />Abimelek amaakaa ke tọwa ado anyʌñ akenwana ye ammọ. Ado ke ini anye akesañake akpere anyenusʌñ tọwa adisịn ikañ ke esịd, <verse eid="JDG 9:52" /><verse number="53" style="v" sid="JDG 9:53" />awonwaan keed amaatop udob itiad ukọkñkpọ tọwa adot ke iwuod Abimelek anyʌñ asuan anye ñkpọkpọrọ.<verse eid="JDG 9:53" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="54" style="v" sid="JDG 9:54" />Ke usọp anye amaakoot akama ñkpọ ekọñ amọ abo, “Dʌt akañkañ mfo sio nyʌñ ñwot miin, mbaak ammọ edibo ‘Awonwaan akewot anye.’ ” Ndin ayịnufọk amọ amaakịm anye ke ufọọd iba ndin anye amaakpa <verse eid="JDG 9:54" /><verse number="55" style="v" sid="JDG 9:55" />Ke ini mbon Isrel ekekịtte ke Abimelek amaakpa, ammọ emaenyọñ ufọk.<verse eid="JDG 9:55" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="56" style="v" sid="JDG 9:56" />Ntom ke Abasi akesio usiene ke ibak A-Abimelek akenamma ye ete amọ ke anye adikiwoot nditọete amọ awo ata mme duob (70). <verse eid="JDG 9:56" /><verse number="57" style="v" sid="JDG 9:57" />Abasi amaanyʌñ anam mbon Sekem ekpe isob ke afịd ndiọi ido ammọ. Isuuñọ Yọtam ayịn Yerub-Baal amaadoro ammọ ke idem.<verse eid="JDG 9:57" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JDG 9" />
  <chapter number="10" style="c" sid="JDG 10" />
  <para style="s1">Tola</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JDG 10:1" />Ke ini Abimelek amaakeboiyo, awo Isaka a-akereke Tola ayịn Pua, ayịn Dodo, amaadakka ada adinyaaña Isrel. Anye akedʌñ ke Samia, ke abod-abod idʌñ Ifrem. <verse eid="JDG 10:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JDG 10:2" />Anye amaadat Isrel usʌñ ke isua edịb mme ita; ndin mbemiso anye akpa, ndin emaebuuk anye ke Samia.<verse eid="JDG 10:2" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yai</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="JDG 10:3" />Andikikeene anye akedo Yai ke Kilied, a-akedatta Isrel usʌñ ke isua edịb mme iba. <verse eid="JDG 10:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JDG 10:4" />Anye akenie nditọ ideen edịb mme duob, e-ekewatta dọñki edịb mme duob. Ammọ ekese ñkpọ ebaña abio edịb mme duob ke Kilied, a-adooho tutu mfịn akere Hafọd Yai. <verse eid="JDG 10:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JDG 10:5" />Ke Yai amaakekpa, emaebuuk anye ke Kamọn.<verse eid="JDG 10:5" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yefta</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="JDG 10:6" />Ini keed mfen mbon Isrel emaenam se idiọọk ke iso Abọọñ. Ammọ emaekpono Baal ye mme Astọred, ye mme abasi Aram, mme abasi Sidọn, mme abasi Mọb, mme abasi Amọn ye mme abasi Filistia. Ndin sia nditọ Isrel emaesịn Abọọñ inyʌññọ inam ñkpọ inọ anye aba, <verse eid="JDG 10:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JDG 10:7" />Abọọñ amaayat esịd ye mbon Isrel. Anye amaayaak ammọ asịn ke ubọk mbon Filistia ye mbon Amọn, <verse eid="JDG 10:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JDG 10:8" />e-ekesuakkake enyʌñ efiik ammọ eboom ke isua ado. Ke ufañ isua duob mme itiaita ammọ emaefiik nditọ Isrel ke edem usakkautịn Yọdan ke Kilied, ke isọñ mme Amọọ. <verse eid="JDG 10:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JDG 10:9" />Mbon Amọn emaenyʌñ efrọ Yọdan ekaa ekenwana ye Yuda, Benyamin ye Ifrem. Isrel akeba ke ekamba mfịna. <verse eid="JDG 10:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JDG 10:10" />Ndin nditọ Isrel emaeseeme enọ Abọọñ ebo, “Ñnyịn imiinam se idiọọk ye afo, imiduọọk Abasi ñnyịn inyʌñ inam ñkpọ Baal.”<verse eid="JDG 10:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="JDG 10:11" />Ndin Abọọñ amaabọọrọ ammọ, “Ke ini mbon Iyib, Amọọ, Amọn, Filistia, <verse eid="JDG 10:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JDG 10:12" />mbon Sidọn, mbon Amalek ye mbon Maon emaifiik ndufo, ndin ndufo emaeseeme ennọ miin eyem unwam, nte ami ñkiinyaañake ndufo nsio ke ubọk ammọ? <verse eid="JDG 10:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JDG 10:13" />Ado ndufo emaentop miin eduọk e-enyʌñ ekenam ñkpọ mme abasi mfen, ndin ami ndiinyaañake ndufo aba. <verse eid="JDG 10:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JDG 10:14" />Ikaa ikiiseeme inọ mme abasi a-ndufo ekemekke. Yak ammọ inyaaña ndufo ke ini ebaaha ke mfịna!”<verse eid="JDG 10:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="JDG 10:15" />Ado mbon Isrel emaebo Abọọñ, “Ñnyịn imiinam idiọọk. Nam ye ñnyịn se adodo a-afo akereke abo ke a-afọn, ado mbọk inyaaña ñnyịn idahami.” <verse eid="JDG 10:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JDG 10:16" />Ndin ammọ emaesioño mme isen abasi ke atu ammọ efep enyʌñ enam ñkpọ enọ Abọọñ. Akem anye ikiikanna adime ukuud Isrel aba.<verse eid="JDG 10:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="JDG 10:17" />Ke ini mbon Amọn ekenama nnaaekọñ ke Kilied adinwana ye Isrel, nditọ Isrel emaeboho itie keed enyʌñ enam nnaaekọñ ke Mispa. <verse eid="JDG 10:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JDG 10:18" />Mme adaiwuod ke Kilied emaedọkkọ emọ-emọ ete, “Awo akeedodo a-adiidat usʌñ ke adinwana ye mbon Amọn ayaado adaiwuod anọ afịd mbon se idʌñọ ke Kilied.”<verse eid="JDG 10:18" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JDG 10" />
  <chapter number="11" style="c" sid="JDG 11" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JDG 11:1" />Yefta awo Kilied akedo uko ke ekọñ. Ete amọ akedo awo Kilied; eka amọ akedo akpara. <verse eid="JDG 11:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JDG 11:2" />Anwaan Kilied amaanyʌñ aman nditọ ideen anọ anye, ndin ke ammọ emaekekpoon iwuọñọ, ammọ emaebịne Yefta esio. Ammọ emaebo anye “Afo uduunieghe udeeme akpa ke ufọk ñnyịn, sia afo ado ayịn awonwaan mfen.” <verse eid="JDG 11:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JDG 11:3" />Ndin Yefta amaafeghe akpọñ nditọete amọ anyʌñ akedʌñ ke isọñ Tob, ke itie a-mme atịme-atịme ibon ekedianake ye anye enyʌñ ekeene anye.<verse eid="JDG 11:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="JDG 11:4" />Ke ini amaakeboiyo, ke ini mbon Amọn ekenwanake ye Isrel, <verse eid="JDG 11:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JDG 11:5" />mme ñkpisọñ ke Kilied emaekaa ekeyem Yefta ke isọñ Tob adinwana ye mbon Isrel. <verse eid="JDG 11:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JDG 11:6" />Ammọ emaebo Yefta “Dido adaiso inọọ ñnyịn, mbaak ñnyịn ikeme adinwana ye mbon Amọn.”<verse eid="JDG 11:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="JDG 11:7" />Yefta amaabo mme adaaha Kilied, “Nte ndufo ikiinsuaha miin inyʌñ imbịne miin isio ke ufọk ete mmi? Nsoo ido yak ndufo edi embịne miin idahami, ke ini ndufo ebaaha ke mfịna?”<verse eid="JDG 11:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="JDG 11:8" />Mme ñkpisọñ ke Kilied emaebo Yefta, “Kpayeado, ñnyịn imiitịmme ubịne fiin idahami, di nọ ñnyịn ikinwana ye mbon Amọn, ndin afo ayaado adaiwuod inọ ñnyịn se idʌñọ ke Kilied.”<verse eid="JDG 11:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="JDG 11:9" />Yefta amaabọọrọ mme adaaha Kilied abo, “Ndufo ekpendat miin nọ ñkenwana ye mbon Amọn ndin Abọọñ ayaak ammọ ansịn miin ke ubọk, nte ke akpanikọ ami ñyaasʌk ndo adaiwuod ndufo?”<verse eid="JDG 11:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="JDG 11:10" />Mme ñkpisọñ abio Kilied emaebọọrọ Yefta ete, “<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ado ntiense ñnyịn; ñnyịn idiitreke adinam se afo atañ.” <verse eid="JDG 11:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JDG 11:11" />Ndin Yefta amaakeene mme ñkpisọñ Kilied, ndin ammọ emaenam anye ado adaiwuod ye adaiso ekọñ ammọ. Anye amaatịmme atañ afịd mme ikọ amọ ke iso Abọọñ ke Mispa.<verse eid="JDG 11:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="JDG 11:12" />Ndin Yefta amaadọñ mme isʌñutom anọ adidem mbon Amọn ye mbuume: “Nsoo utọk ke afo anie ye ami nọ afo anwana ye idịd mmi?”<verse eid="JDG 11:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="JDG 11:13" />Adidem mbon Amọn amaabọọrọ isʌñutom Yefta ate, “Ke ini Isrel ekewuọñọke ke Iyib edọọk edi, ammọ emaeben isọñ mmi ke Anọn tutu ke Yabọk, tutu akewuọ Yọdan. Idahami yaak anye nnọ miin ke emem.”<verse eid="JDG 11:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="JDG 11:14" />Yefta amaatịmme adọñ mme isʌñutom anọ adidem mbon Amọn, <verse eid="JDG 11:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JDG 11:15" />abo:</para>
  <para style="pm" vid="JDG 11:15">“Ami ado se Yefta abo: Isrel ikidatta isọñ Mọb me isọñ mbon Amọn. <verse eid="JDG 11:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JDG 11:16" />Ado ke ini ammọ ekewuọñọke ke Iyib edọọk edi, Isrel ekesaña eboiyo ke anaan esịm ke Ndad-Ndad Akpainyañ enyʌñ ekaa Kades. <verse eid="JDG 11:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JDG 11:17" />Ndin Isrel emaedọñ mme isʌñutom enọ adidem Edọm, ebo, ‘Inọ ñnyịn unen adisaña mboiyo ke idʌñ mfo,’ ado adidem Edọm ikiinyịmmeke. Ammọ emaenyʌñ edọñ enọ adidem Mọb, anye ñko ikinyịmmeke. Ndin Isrel emaesọñ eba ke Kades.<verse eid="JDG 11:17" /></para>
  <para style="pm">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="JDG 11:18" />“Akema ammọ emaesaña eboiyo ke anaan, ekekanna eboiyo ke mben Edọm ye Mọb, eboiyo ke ñkañ edem usakkautịn idʌñ Mọb, enyʌñ enam itie nnaa ke edem Anọn ñkañ uko. Ammọ ikidʌkkọ idʌñ mbon Mọb, sia Anọn akedo adaña ammọ.<verse eid="JDG 11:18" /></para>
  <para style="pm">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="JDG 11:19" />“Ndin nditọ Isrel emaedọñ isʌñutom enọ Sihọn adidem mbon Amọọ, a-akekarake ke Hesbọn, enyʌñ ebo anye, ‘Yak ñnyịn iboiyo ke idʌñ mfo ika itie ñnyịn,’ <verse eid="JDG 11:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JDG 11:20" />Sihọn, naña akeba, ikiinieghe mbuọdidem ke nditọ Isrel adiboiyo ke idʌñ amọ. Ke ntoro anye amaakoot afịd udịmekọñ amọ abon anyʌñ anam nnaaekọñ ke Yahas, anyʌñ anwana ye Isrel.<verse eid="JDG 11:20" /></para>
  <para style="pm">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="JDG 11:21" />“Ado Abọọñ, Abasi Isrel, amaaben Sihọn ye afịd mbon ekọñ amọ asịn ke ubọk Isrel, ammọ emaenyʌñ ekan ammọ. Ndin Isrel amaadat afịd isọñ mbon Amọọ ekedʌññọ ke idʌñ ado, <verse eid="JDG 11:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JDG 11:22" />edat afịd isọñ mbon Amọọ tọọñọ ke Anọn tutu akesịm Yabọk anyʌñ ato ke anaan akesịm Yọdan.<verse eid="JDG 11:22" /></para>
  <para style="pm">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="JDG 11:23" />“Idahami sia Abọọñ Abasi Isrel, abịne mbon Amọọ asioño ke iso ikọd amọ Isrel, nsoo utọ unen ke afo anie adiitịmme ndat anye? <verse eid="JDG 11:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JDG 11:24" />Nte afo ukpuudatta se abasi mfo Kemos unọọ fiin? Ke ukem-ukem ado, se adodo <char style="nd">A-Abọọñ</char> Abasi ñnyịn inọọhọ ñnyịn, ana ñnyịn idat inie. <verse eid="JDG 11:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JDG 11:25" />Nte aba usʌñ a-afo afọnnọ akan Balak ayịn Sipọọ, adidem Mọb? Nte akenaanam anye a-atọhọ ye Isrel me anwana ye ammọ? <verse eid="JDG 11:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="JDG 11:26" />Ke ufañ isua ikie ita (300) ake Isrel ekedʌñọ ke Hesbọn, Arowa, ñkanñkʌk etək idʌñ ye afịd mme abio ke usʌñ Anọn, ntak a-afo uduukutịmmeke udat ammọ ke ini ado-o? <verse eid="JDG 11:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="JDG 11:27" />Ami unamma fiin idiọọk, ado afo amennam miin idiọọk ke adiitịppe ekọñ ye ami. Yak Abọọñ, Akpeikpe, abiide utọk ke ufọọd mbon Isrel ye mbon Amọn mfịn ami.”<verse eid="JDG 11:27" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="JDG 11:28" />Adidem mbon Amọn, kpayeado, ikiikpañña utọñ inọ etob a-Yefta akedọññọ anọ anye.<verse eid="JDG 11:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="JDG 11:29" />Ndin Sịbidịd Abọọñ amaadoro Yefta ke idem. Anye amaafrọ ke Kilied ye Manase, aboiyo ke Mispa ke Kilied, ndin ke itie ado anye amaabịmme abịne mbon Amọn. <verse eid="JDG 11:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="JDG 11:30" />Akem Yefta amaanam akaaña anọ Abọọñ anyʌñ abo: “Adieke afo uduuyaak mbon Amọn unsịn miin ke ubọk, <verse eid="JDG 11:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="JDG 11:31" />se idodo adiiwuọ ke usʌñ ufọk mmi idiisoobo ye ami ke ami mmaakekan mbon Amọn adiinie Abọọñ, ndin ñyaawa anye nte ufọfọb uwa.”<verse eid="JDG 11:31" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="JDG 11:32" />Akem Yefta amaadakka akaa akenwana ye mbon Amọn, ndin Abọọñ amaayaak ammọ asịn anye ke ubọk. <verse eid="JDG 11:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="JDG 11:33" />Anye amaabiat abio edịb tọọñọ ke Aroe tutu akewuọ ñkanñkʌk Minịd, adat akesịm ke Ebeel Keramịm. Ntom ke Isrel akesuuhọ Amọn.<verse eid="JDG 11:33" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="JDG 11:34" />Ke ini Yefta aketịmmeke anyọñ ufọk amọ ke Mispa, adiaha amọ amaawuọ adiisoobo ye anye, asʌk anek unek ke uyio mme ñkukwak! Anye akedo ukweeñe ayịn amọ. Ke amaaboiyo ke anye, Yefta ikinieghe ayịn awodeen me awonwaan mfen. <verse eid="JDG 11:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="JDG 11:35" />Ke ini anye akekịtte anye, anye amaawai afọñidem amọ anyʌñ atua ayịd ate, “Sai, iyoo, adiaha mmi! Afo amensuuhọ miin itie anyʌñ ambuuñ miin. Ami mmaanam akaaña nnọ Abọọñ a-mmiidiikanna mbiat.”<verse eid="JDG 11:35" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="JDG 11:36" />Anye amaabọọrọ, “Ete mmi, afo amaanọ Abọọñ ikọ mfo. Nam ye ami kpa naña afo akenwọñọ, sia Abọọñ amaakesio usiene ye mme asua mfo, kpa mbon Amọn.” <verse eid="JDG 11:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="JDG 11:37" />Anye amaabo, “Ado nam ebeeñe keed ami nnọ miin. Nnọ miin afiọñ iba yak ñkesaaña ke mme abod ñnyʌñ ntua ye mme ufan mmi, sia tutu amama ami ndiidọọhọ ndọ.”<verse eid="JDG 11:37" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" sid="JDG 11:38" />Yefta amaabo, “Afo amekeme adika.” Ndin amaayaak anye akaa ke ufañ afiọñ iba. Anye ye mme ufan amọ emaedakka ekaa ke anyọñ abod eketua sia anye idiidọọhọ ndọ tutu amama. <verse eid="JDG 11:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="JDG 11:39" />Ke afiọñ iba emaekeboiyo, anye amaatịmme anyọñ abịne ete amọ, ndin anye amaanam ye anye naña anye akekaaña. Ndin anye ikidiọọñọke awodeen.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 11:39">Ido mbon Isrel aketọọñọ mi, <verse eid="JDG 11:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="JDG 11:40" />nte ke kwa isua, ana ubọikpa Isrel ewuọ ke usen inaañ eka ekedia usọrọ adiitoiyo ayịn awonwaan Yefta awo Kilied.<verse eid="JDG 11:40" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JDG 11" />
  <chapter number="12" style="c" sid="JDG 12" />
  <para style="s1">Yefta ye Ifrem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JDG 12:1" />Emaekoot mbon ekọñ Ifrem, ndin ammọ emaeboiyo ekaa ke Safọn. Ammọ emaebo Yefta, “Ntak a-afo akekaaha akenwana ekọñ ye mbon Amọn ndin ukoodo ñnyịn nọ isaña ye afo ikaa-a? Ñnyịn iyaifọp ufọk mfo.”<verse eid="JDG 12:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="JDG 12:2" />Yefta amaabọọrọ abo, “Ami ye mbon mmi imainie ekamba anwan ye mbon Amọn, ndin akpesʌkado ami mmaikoot, ndufo ikiñnyaañake miin isio ke ubọk ammọ. <verse eid="JDG 12:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JDG 12:3" />Ke ini ami ñke akịtte ke ndufo idiiñnwamma miin, ami mmaaben uwem mmi nsịn ke ubọk mmi ñnyʌñ mfrọ ke anwana ye mbon Amọn, ndin Abọọñ amaanam ami ñkan ammọ. Idahami nsoo inam yak ndufo edi embịne miin mfịn edinwana ye ami?”<verse eid="JDG 12:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="JDG 12:4" />Ndin Yefta amaakoot mme ideen ke Kilied abon anyʌñ akenwana ekọñ ye Ifrem. Mbon Kilied emaekan ammọ sia mbon Ifrem ekebo, “Ndufo mbon Kilied edoñño mbon ntịme e-etooho Ifrem ye Manase.” <verse eid="JDG 12:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JDG 12:5" />Mbon Kilied emaedat mme itie mbeghe ke Yọdan a-adatta aka akewuọ Ifrem, ndin ini keed akeedodo a-mbon Ifrem se ikibọkkọ ebooho, “Yak ami mboiyo ñka edem uko,” mbon Kilied emaebịp anye, “Afo ado awo Ifrem?” Adieke anye abọọrọke, “Iyoo,” <verse eid="JDG 12:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JDG 12:6" />ammọ emaebo, “A-afọn, bo ‘Siboled.’ ” Adieke anye akekanna abo, “Siboled,” sia anye imiikikanna ikoot ikọ ado nnen-nnen, ammọ emaemʌm anye enyʌñ ekewot anye ke itie mbeghe Yọdan. Mbon Ifrem awo tọsịn aba mme iba (42,000) ke ekewot ke ini ado.<verse eid="JDG 12:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="JDG 12:7" />Yefta amaadat<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12:7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">amaakpe ikpe; se ñko ke Ñwed Mme Abiideikpe 12:8-14</char></note> Isrel usʌñ ke isua itiokeed. Akem Yefta awo Kilied amaakpa emaenyʌñ ebuuk anye ke abio Kilied.<verse eid="JDG 12:7" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ibsan, Elọn ye Abdọn</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="JDG 12:8" />Yefta amaakekweeñe, Ibsan awo Betlehem amaadat Isrel usʌñ. <verse eid="JDG 12:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JDG 12:9" />Anye akenie nditọ ideen edịb mme duob ye nditọ ibaan edịb mme duob. Anye amaawuọ akpọñ ekpək amọ akenọ nditọ ibaan amọ ndọ, anye amaanyʌñ awuọ akpọñ ekpək amọ akekoono ubọikpa edịb mme duob nte ibaan ndọ anọ nditọ ideen amọ. Ibsan amaadat Isrel usʌñ ke isua itiaba. <verse eid="JDG 12:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JDG 12:10" />Akem Ibsan amaakpa emaenyʌñ ebuuk anye ke Betlehem.<verse eid="JDG 12:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="JDG 12:11" />Anye amaakekweeñe, Elon awo Sebulọn amaadat Isrel usʌñ ke isua duob. <verse eid="JDG 12:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JDG 12:12" />Akem Elon amaakpa emaenyʌñ ebuuk anye ke Aiyalọn ke isọñ Sebulọn.<verse eid="JDG 12:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="JDG 12:13" />Elon amaakekweeñe, Abdọn ayịn Hilel, awo Piratọn, amaadat Isrel usʌñ. <verse eid="JDG 12:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JDG 12:14" />Anye amaanie nditọ ideen aba ye nditọ ayeyịn ideen edịb mme duob, ekewatta ke mme dọñki ata mme duob. Anye amaadat Isrel usʌñ ke isua itiaita. <verse eid="JDG 12:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JDG 12:15" />Akem Abdọn ayịn awodeen Hilel amaakpa emaenyʌñ ebuuk anye ke Piratọn ke Ifrem, ke abod abio mbon Amalek.<verse eid="JDG 12:15" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JDG 12" />
  <chapter number="13" style="c" sid="JDG 13" />
  <para style="s1">Emana Samsịn</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JDG 13:1" />Ini mfen mbon Isrel emaetịmme enam se idiọọk ke iso Abọọñ, ndin Abọọñ amaayaak ammọ asịn ke ubọk mbon Filistia ke isua aba.<verse eid="JDG 13:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="JDG 13:2" />Awo Sora keed, a-akekereke Manoa, a-aketooho ubon Daan, amaanie anwaan a-akedooho ada, a-mmiikikanna iman ayịn. <verse eid="JDG 13:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JDG 13:3" />Akem enyere Abọọñ amaabiọññọ anọ anye anyʌñ abo, “Afo ado ada unyʌññọ unie ayịn, ado afo ayaayommo anyʌñ aman ayịn. <verse eid="JDG 13:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JDG 13:4" />Idahami kịt bo ke afo unwọññọ ukọd ndomokeed me ndañ ukọd; mfen ñko ke afo unyʌññọ udia ñkpọ se imiisanake. <verse eid="JDG 13:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JDG 13:5" />Afo ayaayommo anyʌñ aman ayịn awodeen a-adooho akadañ inaaha atuuk iwuod amọ sia ayịn ado adiido Nasariin, a-anieghe Abasi tọọñọ ke idịb. Anye adiida iso ke adinyaaña Isrel nsio ke ubọk mbon Filistia.”<verse eid="JDG 13:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="JDG 13:6" />Ndin awonwaan ado amaakaa abịne ebe amọ anyʌñ akedọkkọ anye ate, “Awo Abasi keed amaadi ambịne miin. Anye aketie nte enyere Abasi, anie uteeñe eti-eti. Ami ñkibịppe anye itie nte anye aketo adi, anye ikiinyʌññọ indọkkọ miin anyịñ amọ. <verse eid="JDG 13:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JDG 13:7" />Ado anye amaambo miin, ‘Afo ayaayommo anyʌñ aman ayịn awodeen. Idahami ndin, kịt bo ke imọ inwọññọ ukọd me ndañ ukọd; mfen ñko ke unyʌññọ udia ñkpọ ake imiisanake, sia ayịn ado adiido Nasariin a-anieghe Abasi tọọñọ ke idịb tutu usen ñkpa amọ.’ ”<verse eid="JDG 13:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="JDG 13:8" />Ndin Manoa amaabọñ akam anọ Abọọñ ate, “Dakka nọ ayịnufọk mfo, Abọọñ. Ami mmuubeeñe fiin yak anam awo Abasi ado afo akedọññọ inọọ ñnyịn amaana atịmme adikpeep ñnyịn naña idiikama ayịn ado a-adi imana.”<verse eid="JDG 13:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="JDG 13:9" />Abasi amaakop anọ Manoa, ndin enyere Abasi ado amaatịmme adi abịne awonwaan ado ke ini anye akebaaha ke inwañ; ado ebe amọ Manoa ikibaaha ye anye. <verse eid="JDG 13:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JDG 13:10" />Anwaan ado amaasọp isañ akaa aketañ anọ ebe amọ ate, “Anye mmọ mi! Awodeen a-akebiọññọke annọọ miin usen anye ako!”<verse eid="JDG 13:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="JDG 13:11" />Manoa amaadakka ada anyʌñ akeene anwaan amọ. Anye amaakedisịme awodeen ado, anye amaabo, “Nte afo ado awo aketañña ikọ anọọ anwaan mmi?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 13:11">Anye amaabọọrọ ate, “Ami ke ado.”<verse eid="JDG 13:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="JDG 13:12" />Ndin Manoa amaabịp anye ate, “Mme ikọ mfo emaewuọ isu, nsoo idiido mbed a-adiikaara uwem ayịn ami ye ubọkutom amọ?”<verse eid="JDG 13:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="JDG 13:13" />Enyere <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaabọọrọ Manoa, “Anwaan mfo ana nte anam afịd se ami ñkedọkkọ anye. <verse eid="JDG 13:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JDG 13:14" />Inaaha anye adia ñkpọ ndomokeed a-atooho fain, me anwọñ ukọd ndomokeed me ndañ ukọd me adia ñkpọ ndomokeed i-imiisanake. Ana nte anye anam afịd ñkpọ se ntemme anye.”<verse eid="JDG 13:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="JDG 13:15" />Manoa amaabo enyere <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, “Ñnyịn ikpaima afo atie tutu ñnyịn item ñyịn ebod unọ fiin.”<verse eid="JDG 13:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="JDG 13:16" />Enyere Abọọñ amaabọọrọ, “Akpekọm afo ammʌm miin anịm ukad, ami ndiidiaha ndidia mfo ndomokeed. Ado adieke afo anamma ufọfọb uwa, wa anye nọ Abọọñ.” (Manoa ikiidiọọñọke ke anye akedo enyere Abọọñ.)<verse eid="JDG 13:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="JDG 13:17" />Ndin Manoa amaabịp enyere Abọọñ, “Nsoo ido anyịñ mfo, nọ ñnyịn idu ukpono fiin ke ini ikọ mfo awuọhọ asu?”<verse eid="JDG 13:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="JDG 13:18" />Ado enyere Abọọñ amaabọọrọ, “Nsoo inam nọ afo ambịp miin anyịñ mmi? Anye ado ayañña awo ifiọk.” <verse eid="JDG 13:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JDG 13:19" />Ndin Manoa amaaben ñyịn ebod, ye uwa ñkpasi, anyʌñ adoot anye ke itiad awa anọ Abọọñ. Akem Abọọñ amaanam ataa utịppeñkpọ ke ini Manoa ye anwaan amọ ekedaaha ese <verse eid="JDG 13:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JDG 13:20" />naña edemeikañ asak awuọ ke akpokoro uwa adọọk anyọñ, enyere Abọọñ amaadọọk ke edemeikañ ado. Ke ekịtte ami, Manoa ye anwaan amọ emaeduọññọ ekʌp iso ke isọñ. <verse eid="JDG 13:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JDG 13:21" />Ke ini enyere Abọọñ imiikitịmmeke idiwọt Manoa ye anwaan idem amọ, Manoa ndin amaadiọọñọ ke anye akedo enyere Abọọñ.<verse eid="JDG 13:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="JDG 13:22" />Manoa amaadọkkọ anwaan amọ “Ebiere inọ ñnyịn edikpañña! Ñnyịn imikịt Abasi!”<verse eid="JDG 13:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="JDG 13:23" />Ado anwaan amọ amaabọọrọ, “Akpedo Abọọñ amaayem adiwot ñnyịn, anye ikpiikibọọhọ ufọfọb uwa ye uwa mfịd inwañ ke ubọk ñnyịn, me adiwọt ñnyịn afịd mme ñkpọ ami me ñkpọ anye idọkkọke ñnyịn idahami.”<verse eid="JDG 13:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="JDG 13:24" />Ndin awonwaan ami amaaman ayịn awodeen anyʌñ asio anye anyịñ Samsịn. Anye amaakọt ndin Abọọñ amaanyʌñ adiọñ anye, <verse eid="JDG 13:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JDG 13:25" />ndin Sịbidịd Abọọñ amaatọọñọ adibukko anye ke ini anye akebaaha ke Mahane Daan, ke ufọọd Sora ye Estaol.<verse eid="JDG 13:25" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JDG 13" />
  <chapter number="14" style="c" sid="JDG 14" />
  <para style="s1">Ndọ Samsịn</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JDG 14:1" />Akem Samsịn amaasọiyọ akaa Timna anyʌñ akekịt abọikpa Filistia keed. <verse eid="JDG 14:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JDG 14:2" />Anye amaakenyọñ idi, anye amaadọkkọ ete ye eka amọ, “Ami mmekịt awonwaan Filistia ke Timna; ndin idọ anye innọ miin nte anwaan mmi.”<verse eid="JDG 14:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="JDG 14:3" />Ndin ete ye eka amọ emaebọọrọ ete, “Nte awonwaan se ekpedat ibaaha ke atu mbon se iwuana ñkpọ me ke atu afịd mbon ñnyịn? Nte ana afo aka ke atu mbon Filistia ammiifọọrọke edʌd akedat anwaan?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 14:3">Ado Samsịn amaabo ete amọ, “Dọ anye nnọ miin. Anye ado anye a-adotto ye ami.” <verse eid="JDG 14:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JDG 14:4" />(Ete ye eka amọ ikiidiọọñọke ke ami aketo Abọọñ, a-akeyemme ufañ adinam mbon Filistia ñkpọ; sia ke ini ado ammọ ekekaara Isrel.)<verse eid="JDG 14:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="JDG 14:5" />Samsịn amaasaña ye ete ye eka amọ akaa Timna. Idaha ammọ ekpereke inwañ fain Timna, ke ini anye idiikikpeññe anyen ñyịn ekpe amaakuun afeghe abịne anye. <verse eid="JDG 14:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JDG 14:6" />Sịbidịd Abọọñ amaadi ke adudu adidoro anye ke idem ndin anye amaawai ekpe ado mbai-mbai ke ñkaña ubọk amọ nte anye akpewaiya ñyịn ebod. Ado anye ikidọkkọke ete ye eka amọ se anye akenam. <verse eid="JDG 14:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JDG 14:7" />Ndin anye amaasọiyọ akaa anyʌñ akenie nneme ye awonwaan ado, ndin Samsịn ama anye.<verse eid="JDG 14:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="JDG 14:8" />Akekem koo, Samsịn amaatịmme akaa adinam ndọ ye anye, ndin anye amaawọññọ ada ase akpo ekpe ado, anyʌñ akịt eboho akwọọk ye adanakwọọk ke esịd. <verse eid="JDG 14:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JDG 14:9" />Anye amaadat ubọk amọ akoi adanakwọọk anyʌñ adia naña anye akesañake ke usʌñ. Ke ini anye akesịmeke ete ye eka amọ, anye amaanọ ammọ ubaak, ndin ammọ ñko emaenyʌñ edia. Ado anye ikiidọkkọke ammọ ke ikidat anye ito akpo ekpe ado.<verse eid="JDG 14:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="JDG 14:10" />Ete amọ amaakaa adikịt awonwaan ado. Ndin Samsịn amaanam usọrọ ke itie ado, naña ido ñkparawa akesido. <verse eid="JDG 14:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JDG 14:11" />Ke ini mme awo ekekịtte anye, ammọ emaemek awo edịb mme duob adido nsaña amọ.<verse eid="JDG 14:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="JDG 14:12" />Samsịn amaabo ammọ, “Yak ami idọkkọ ndufo ñke keed. Adieke ndufo ekemekke edinnọọ miin ibọọrọ ke ufañ usen itiaba u-usọrọ adiika iso, ami ñyainọ ndufo afọñidem linen edịb mme duob ye ukpʌhọ afọñ edịb mme duob. <verse eid="JDG 14:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JDG 14:13" />Ado adieke ndufo imiikanna indọkkọ miin ibọọrọ, ana nte ndufo ennọ miin afọñidem edịb mme duob ye ukpʌhọ afọñ edịb mme duob.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 14:13">Ammọ emaebo, “Idọkkọ ñnyịn ñke mfo. Nam ñnyịn ikop anye.”<verse eid="JDG 14:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="JDG 14:14" />Anye amaabọọrọ,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="JDG 14:14">“Aketo ke adia ñkpọ, ñkpọ se edia awuọ;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 14:14">aketo ke akpọsọñ, inịññe ñkpọ awuọ.”</para>
  <para style="m" vid="JDG 14:14">Ke idak usen ita ammọ ikiikanna inọ ibọọrọ.<verse eid="JDG 14:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="JDG 14:15" />Ke ayọhọ usen inaañ, ammọ emaebo anwaan Samsịn, “Kpek ebe mfo nọ anye akappa ñke ado inọ ñnyịn, imiidooho ñnyịn iyaufọp fiin ye mbon ufọk ete mfo iwoot. Nte afo akiikoot ñnyịn adi mi nọ ediyịp inie ñnyịn?”<verse eid="JDG 14:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="JDG 14:16" />Ndin anwaan Samsịn amaatop idem adot Samsịn ke idem, atua, “Afo ansuasua miin! Afo unekkeke umma miin. Afo amaatop ñke anọ mbon mmi, ado afo ukusiaha ibọọrọ unnọ miin.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 14:16">Anye amaabọọrọ, “Ami ñkappake ñke ado nnọ ete ye eka mmi, ndin ntak a-ami ñkpekappake unọ fiin-e?” <verse eid="JDG 14:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JDG 14:17" />Ndin anwaan Samsịn amaatua ke afịd usen itiaba usọrọ ado. Akem ke ayọhọ usen itiaba Samsịn amaadọkkọ anye, sia anye amaakaa iso anyịk anye. Anye ke idem amọ amaakanna aketañ se ñke ado awuọñọ anọ mbon amọ.<verse eid="JDG 14:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="JDG 14:18" />Mbemiso utịn asop ke ayọhọ usen itiaba mbon abio ado emaebo anye,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="JDG 14:18">“Nsoo ñkpọ inịññe ikan adanakwọọk?</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 14:18">Nsoo ñkpọ isọñ adudu ikan ekpe?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 14:18">Samsịn amaabo ammọ,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="JDG 14:18">“Akpedo ndufo ikifʌññọ isọñ ye ñyịn umanenañ mmi,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 14:18">ndufo ikpisiaha ñke mmi.”<verse eid="JDG 14:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="JDG 14:19" />Ndin Sịbidịd Abọọñ amaadi ke adudu adidoro anye ke idem. Anye amaakaa Askelọn, akewot ideen ammọ awo edịb mme duob, abọi ammọ afịdñkpọ anyʌñ ayaak anọ mbon se ikikappa ñke ado. Ke ufiob iyadesịd, anye amaatịmme anyọñ ufọk ete amọ. <verse eid="JDG 14:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JDG 14:20" />Ndin emaeben anwaan Samsịn enọ keed ke atu mbon ekesañake ye anye ke ini usọrọ ado.<verse eid="JDG 14:20" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JDG 14" />
  <chapter number="15" style="c" sid="JDG 15" />
  <para style="s1">Samsịn Asio Mbon Filistia Usiene</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JDG 15:1" />Ke ini ukpịkke abakpa, Samsịn amaaben ñyịn ebod akaa adikise anwaan amọ. Anye amaabo, “Ami ñyem adika ubeed anwaan mmi.” Ado ete anwaan ikiinyịmmeke anye adʌk.<verse eid="JDG 15:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="JDG 15:2" />Anye amaabo, “Ami mmaanekke ndiọọñọ mbo ke afo asuasua anye, ndin ami mmaaben anye nnọ nsaña mfo. Nte etək ayịneka amọ awonwaan iyaiyake ikan anye? Dat anye ado ke itie amọ.”<verse eid="JDG 15:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="JDG 15:3" />Samsịn amaabo ammọ, “Ami mmenie ufañ idaha ami adinekke nsio mbon Filistia usiene; ami ñyaanekke nnọmọ ammọ.” <verse eid="JDG 15:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JDG 15:4" />Ndin anye amaakemʌm ewaikọd ikie ita (300) anyʌñ abọp ammọ iba-iba ke isịm. Akem anye amaabọp ikañ emuum adian ke isịm ammọ, <verse eid="JDG 15:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JDG 15:5" />asʌm ikañ ayịt ke mme ikañ emuum ado anyʌñ asaana ammọ ayaak ke inwañ abakpa mbon Filistia. Ntom ke anye akefọp mme eboho abakpa ekekpịkkeke ye mbon edaahada, adian ye inwañ fain ye inwañ ọlif.<verse eid="JDG 15:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="JDG 15:6" />Ke ini mbon Filistia ekebịppe, “Anie awo akenam ñkpọ ami?” emaedọkkọ ammọ, “Samsịn, ebe ayịn awo Timna, ke ntak a-adooho emaeben anwaan amọ enọ awo nsaña amọ.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 15:6">Ndin mbon Filistia emaekaa ekefọp awonwaan ado ye ete amọ ewot. <verse eid="JDG 15:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JDG 15:7" />Samsịn amaabo ammọ, “Sia ndufo enamma ntom, ami mmenwọñọ mbo ke ndiitreke adisio ndufo usiene.” <verse eid="JDG 15:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JDG 15:8" />Ndin anye amaatịppe ekọñ idiọọk-idiọọk ye ammọ anyʌñ awot uwak ammọ. Akem anye amaakaa akedʌñ ke abaitiad ke Etam.<verse eid="JDG 15:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="JDG 15:9" />Mbon Filistia emaedọọk ekenam nnaaekọñ ke Yuda, esuana ekaa ñkpere Lehi. <verse eid="JDG 15:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JDG 15:10" />Mbon Yuda emaebịp, “Nsoo ido ntak a-ndufo ediighe inwana ye ñnyịn?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 15:10">Ammọ emaebọọrọ ebo, “Ñnyịn ikidi adiben Samsịn nte awo ñkpakọb, adinam ye anye se anye akenam ye ñnyịn.”<verse eid="JDG 15:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="JDG 15:11" />Akem awo ikie ita ke Yuda emaekaa ke abaitiad ke Etam ekebo Samsịn, “Nte afo udiọọñọke ke mbon Filistia edo mme andikara ñnyịn? Nsoo ke afo anam ami ye ñnyịn?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 15:11">Anye amaabọọrọ abo, “Ami ñkenam ammọ kpa se ammọ ekennam miin.”<verse eid="JDG 15:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="JDG 15:12" />Ammọ emaebo anye, “Ñnyịn ikidi adubọp fiin ñnyʌñ uben fiin ñyaak nnọọ mbon Filistia.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 15:12">Samsịn amaabo ammọ, “Inwọñọ innọ miin ibo ke ndufo idiiñwotto miin ke idem ndufo.”<verse eid="JDG 15:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="JDG 15:13" />Ammọ emaebọọrọ, “Imiinyịmme, ñnyịn iduubọbọp fiin kpọd inyʌñ usaana fiin iyaak inọ ammọ. Ñnyịn iduuwotto fiin.” Ndin ammọ emaebọp anye ke ufa idʌk iba enyʌñ eben anye esio ke abaitiad. <verse eid="JDG 15:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JDG 15:14" />Nte ammọ ekaaha ke Lehi, mbon Filistia emaesio ñkpo edi ebịne anye. Sịbidịd Abọọñ amaadi adudu-adudu adidoro anye ke idem. Ndin udʌk ke ubọk amọ amaabeghe akappa atie nte flaks e-efọppọ ke ikañ, anyʌñ akpọhọ ke ubọk amọ. <verse eid="JDG 15:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JDG 15:15" />Ke ini Samsịn akannake anyen akịt akpọmbañ dọñki anye amaaben awoot mme awo tọsịn keed (1,000).<verse eid="JDG 15:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="JDG 15:16" />Ndin Samsịn amaabo,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="JDG 15:16">“Ami mmedat akpọmbañ dọñki keed</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 15:16">nnam ammọ edo mme dọñki.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="JDG 15:16">Ami mmedat akpọmbañ dọñki keed</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 15:16">ñwot ideen tọsịn keed.”<verse eid="JDG 15:16" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="JDG 15:17" />Ke ini anye akweeñeke se aketañ, anye amaatop akpọmbañ ado aduọk, ndin ekekoot itie ado Ramad Lehi.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15:17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ramad Lehi awuọñọ abio me abod.</char></note><verse eid="JDG 15:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="JDG 15:18" />Sia anye amaanekke akop nsaditọñ, anye amaatua aseeme anọ Abọọñ, “Afo amenọ ayịnufọk mfo utọ ekamba adikan ami. Nte ana ami ñkpa idahami ke ntak nsaditọñ ñnyʌñ nduọ ndʌk ke ubọk mbon ammiifọọrọke edʌd?” <verse eid="JDG 15:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JDG 15:19" />Ndin Abasi amaatịppe adudu ke isọñ Lehi, mmọọñ amaanyʌñ awuọñọ. Ke ini Samsịn amaakenwọñ mmọọñ, adudu amọ amaatịmme ademme. Ndin emaekoot idịm ado En Hakọre, ndin anye mmọdo asʌk aba ke Lehi.<verse eid="JDG 15:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="JDG 15:20" />Samsịn amaadat Isrel usʌñ ke isua edịb ke ini mbon Filistia.<verse eid="JDG 15:20" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JDG 15" />
  <chapter number="16" style="c" sid="JDG 16" />
  <para style="s1">Samsịn ye Delaila</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JDG 16:1" />Usen keed Samsịn amaakaa Kasa, ke itie ado anye amaakịt akpara keed anyʌñ akena ye anye ke akonayio ado. <verse eid="JDG 16:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JDG 16:2" />Emaedọkkọ mbon Kasa ete, “Samsịn mmọ mi!” Ammọ emaekanna itie ado ekʌk enyʌñ etie ebet anye ke afịd akonayio ke inuaatob abio. Ammọ ikinyekkeke idem ke afịd akonayio ado, sia ekebo, “Ke usiere ñnyịn iyaiwot anye.”<verse eid="JDG 16:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="JDG 16:3" />Ado Samsịn amaanaa do tutu ke ufọọd akonayio. Ndin Samsịn amaadakka ada anyʌñ amʌm usʌñ inuaatob abio, adian ye abọọk iba, anyʌñ akpọk ammọ awịppe, eto ibiọñ ye afịd ñkpọ. Anye amaadịppe ammọ adoot ke mme afara amọ anyʌñ aben ammọ akaa ke iwuod abod adaaha ase Hibrọn.<verse eid="JDG 16:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="JDG 16:4" />Akekem koo, Samsịn amaatọọñọ ima ye awonwaan keed ke Itịkke Sorek, a-anyịñ amọ akedooho Delaila. <verse eid="JDG 16:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JDG 16:5" />Mme andikara Filistia emaekaa ebịne awonwaan ado ekebo, “Se ise naña afo akpekan atap anye yak anye utemme fiin ndedịbe se isịne ke akpọsọñ adudu amọ ye naña ñnyịn ikpikan anye ubọk ndin ibọp anye inyʌñ isuuk anye inịm. Ñnyịn awo keedekeed iyaunọ fiin sekel<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16:5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ñkpọ nte kilokram 13</char></note> silfa ikie duob mme keed (1,100).”<verse eid="JDG 16:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="JDG 16:6" />Ndin Delaila amaabo Samsịn, “Ndọkkọ miin ndedịbe ñkpọ a-asịneke ke akpọsọñ adudu mfo ye naña ekpekan ubọp fiin enịm enyʌñ ukan fiin.”<verse eid="JDG 16:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="JDG 16:7" />Samsịn amaabọọrọ anye ate, “Adieke awo ambọppọ miin ke ndisi idʌk utịgha itiaba ake awo imiinwanna yak asat, ami ñyaakappa mmem nte mme ideen mfen.”<verse eid="JDG 16:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="JDG 16:8" />Ndin mme andikara Filistia emaedat ndisi idʌk utịgha itiaba ake awo imiinwanna yak asat esọk anye, ndin Delaila amaadat ammọ abọp Samsịn. <verse eid="JDG 16:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JDG 16:9" />Mme awo emaekedịbe ke ubeed, ndin Delaila amaakoot anye, “Samsịn, mbon Filistia eyaumʌm fiin!” Ado anye amaakịp mme idʌk ado ñkeñe-ñkeñe nte idʌk akpekịppe ke ini ebenne ekpere edemeikañ. Ke ntoro awo ikidiọọñọke nte ndịbe adudu amọ ato.<verse eid="JDG 16:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="JDG 16:10" />Ndin Delaila amaabo Samsịn, “Afo amenam ami ndo ndisịme; afo amaasʌhọ nsu annọ miin. Idahami, ndọkkọ miin naña ekeme adubọp fiin.”<verse eid="JDG 16:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="JDG 16:11" />Anye amaabo, “Adieke awo akeedodo ambọppọ miin nọ anekke asọñ ke mme ufa idʌk ake awo imiidatta ibọp ñkpọ akpa, ami ñyaakappa mmem kpa nte awodeen mfen.”<verse eid="JDG 16:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="JDG 16:12" />Ndin Delaila amaadat mme ufa idʌk abọp anye. Akem, anye amaakoot mme ideen awo ekedịbeke ke ubeed, ate, “Samsịn, mbon Filistia eyaumʌm fiin!” Ado anye amaakịp mme idʌk ado asio ke ubọk amọ nte udʌk ukịm afọñ.<verse eid="JDG 16:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="JDG 16:13" />Akem Delaila amaabo Samsịn, “Awuọñọ ke afịd ini ami afo akesiñkama miin anam ndisịme anyʌñ asʌhọ nsu annọ miin. Ndọkkọ miin ndin naña ekeme adubọp fiin.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 16:13">Samsịn amaabọọrọ, “Adieke afo adọkkọ ided iwuod mmi naña itiaba nte afọñ, akama abiaween amʌm anye yak asọñ, ami ñyaakappa mmem nte mme ideen mfen.” Ndin ke ini anye akedaiyake, Delaila amaaben udọdọk ided itiaba ke iwuod amọ, adọk ammọ akịm adian ke afọñ <verse eid="JDG 16:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JDG 16:14" />anyʌñ abọp anye awuuk abiaween.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 16:14">Ini keed mfen anye amaakoot anye, “Samsịn, mbon Filistia eyaumʌm fiin!” Anye amaademme ke idab anyʌñ adʌt abiaween ye udọdọk ided, adiañña ye afọñ adịppe asio.<verse eid="JDG 16:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="JDG 16:15" />Ndin anye amaabo anye, “Afo anam die abo, ‘Ami mmuma fiin,’ ke ini afo umuutañña ndịbe ñkpọ unnọ miin? Ayọhọ akañ ita ado ami a-afo andatta miin anam ndisịme, unyʌññọ undọkkọ miin ndedịbe ñkpọ a-asịneke ke akpọsọñ adudu mfo.” <verse eid="JDG 16:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JDG 16:16" />Delaila amaakama akpọsọñ utañ ikọ ayịre anye ke usen ke usen tutu anye ikanna iyọ aba.<verse eid="JDG 16:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="JDG 16:17" />Ndin anye amaadọkkọ Delaila afịd ñkpọ, abo “Akenaanam akadañ ndomokeed idʌkkọ iwuod mmi, sia ami ndo Nasariin e-ekeyaaha enọ Abasi tọọñọ ke idịb eka mmi. Adieke efatta ided ke iwuod mmi, adudu mmi ayañkpọñ miin, ndin ami ñyaakappa mmem kpa nte awodeen mfen.”<verse eid="JDG 16:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="JDG 16:18" />Ke ini Delaila akekịtte abo ke anye amaidọkkọ imọ afịd ñkpọ, anye amaadọñ utom anọ mme andikara Filistia, “Itịmme idi ini keed mfen; anye andọkkọ miin afịd ñkpọ.” Ndin mme andikara Filistia emaetịmme edi ye akʌk ke ubọk ammọ. <verse eid="JDG 16:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JDG 16:19" />Ke Delaila amaakenam Samsịn adaiya ke ifʌkkọ amọ, anye amaakoot awo yak adifat anye udọdọk ided itiaba amọ asioño, ndin inweek amọ amaatọọñọ asuuhọ. Ndin adudu amọ amaakpọñ anye.<verse eid="JDG 16:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="JDG 16:20" />Akem anye amaakoot, “Samsịn, mbon Filistia eyaumʌm fiin!”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 16:20">Anye amaademme ke idab anyʌñ akere. “Ami ñyaawuọ ñkaa naña ñkesiwuọ ñnyʌñ mfiọnnọ mbọkkọ.” Ado anye ikiidiọọñọke ke Abọọñ amaakpọñ anye.<verse eid="JDG 16:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="JDG 16:21" />Akem mbon Filistia emaemʌm anye, etʌññọ anye naña anyen iba enyʌñ eben anye ekaa Kasa. Emaebọp anye ke ñkpọnọ brọns, enyʌñ enam anye nọ asikọk ñkpasi ke ufọk ñkpakọb. <verse eid="JDG 16:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JDG 16:22" />Ado ided ke iwuod amọ amaamaana atọọñọ atịppe ke emaekefat.<verse eid="JDG 16:22" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ñkpa Samsịn</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="JDG 16:23" />Ndin mme adaiwuod ke Filistia emaesoobo idem adiwa ekamba uwa nnọọ Dakọn abasi ammọ ñnyʌñ ndia idaara, ete, “Abasi ñnyịn amaayaak Samsịn, asua ñnyịn, isịn ñnyịn ke ubọk.”<verse eid="JDG 16:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="JDG 16:24" />Ke ini mme awo ekekịtte Samsịn, ammọ emaetooro abasi ammọ, ete,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="JDG 16:24">“Abasi ñnyịn a-ayaak asua ñnyịn</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 16:24">isịn ñnyịn ke ubọk,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="JDG 16:24">anye a-abiada isọñ ñnyịn</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="JDG 16:24">anyʌñ anam ñkpañña ñnyịn atọt.”<verse eid="JDG 16:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="JDG 16:25" />Ke ini ammọ ekebaaha ke ekamba inemesịd, ammọ emaesio ñkpo ete, “Iben Samsịn idi yak adibre mbre inọ ñnyịn.” Ndin ammọ emaekoot Samsịn esio ke ufọk ñkpakọb, anye amaanyʌñ abre mbre anọ ammọ.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 16:25">Ke ini ekedaahake anye ekpere mme abai, <verse eid="JDG 16:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="JDG 16:26" />Samsịn amaabo ayịnufọk a-akemʌmmọ anye ubọk, “Ndaaha miin ke itie se ndiikan ntuuk mme abai e-emʌmmọ tembịd ekama, nọ ami ñkeme adiibere ke ammọ.” <verse eid="JDG 16:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="JDG 16:27" />Idaha ntoro, tembịd amaayọhọ ye ideen ye ibaan; afịd mme andikara Filistia emaeba do, ndin ke anyọñ akọm ufọk ñkpọ nte awo tọsịn ita (3,000) ideen ye ibaan emaetie ese naña Samsịn asio mbre. <verse eid="JDG 16:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="JDG 16:28" />Akem Samsịn amaabọñ akam <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, “<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikara, ntoiyo miin. Mbọk, Abasi, nnọ miin adudu kpa ini keed mfen, ndin yak ndat ubọketa keed nsio mbon Filistia usiene ke anyen mmi iba.” <verse eid="JDG 16:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="JDG 16:29" />Akem Samsịn amaasaña akemuum mme abai iba ekedaaha ke ufọọd tembịd akama. Ke abenne idem amọ adian ke ammọ, ubọk nnasia amọ ke keed, ubọk ufiin ke anye ako, <verse eid="JDG 16:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="JDG 16:30" />Samsịn amaabo, “Yak ami ñkpa ye mbon Filistia!” Ndin anye amaanək ke afịd inweek amọ, ndin tembịd amaawuuro afʌk mme andikara ye afịd mbon awo se ikidọñọ ke esịd. Ntoro ke anye akewot mbon awo se iwak ke ini anye akekpaaha akan ke ayio uwem amọ.<verse eid="JDG 16:30" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="JDG 16:31" />Akem mme nditọeka amọ ye afịd ufọk ete amọ emaekaa ekeben anye. Ammọ emaeben anye enyọñ enyʌñ ekebuuk anye ke ufọọd Sora ye Estaol ke udi Manoa ete amọ. Anye amaadat<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16:31 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">amaakpe ikpe</char></note> Isrel usʌñ ke isua edịb.<verse eid="JDG 16:31" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JDG 16" />
  <chapter number="17" style="c" sid="JDG 17" />
  <para style="s1">Mme Isen Abasi Maika</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JDG 17:1" />Akekem awo keed a-akekereke Maika ke abod abio Ifrem, <verse eid="JDG 17:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JDG 17:2" />amaabo eka amọ, “Sekel silfa ikie duob mme keed (1,100)<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">17:2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ñkpọ nte kilokram 13</char></note> ado ekuubọọhọ fiin do, a-ami ñkekoppo naña afo asịn isuuñọ, mmọdo aba ye ami; ami ñkeben anye.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 17:2">Akem eka amọ amaabo, “<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> udiọñ fiin, ayịn mmi!”<verse eid="JDG 17:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="JDG 17:3" />Ke ini anye akebenne sekel silfa ikie duob mme keed (1,100) akenọ eka amọ, eka amọ amaabo, “Ami ke ayọhọ ukpono mmeyaak silfa mmi nnọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> nọ ayịn mmi adat anam usọ mbid awo e-edatta silfa enam. Ñyaatịmme ñyaak anye unọ fiin.”<verse eid="JDG 17:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="JDG 17:4" />Ndin ke anye amaaketịmme akenọ eka amọ silfa ado, eka amọ amaaben sekel silfa ikie iba (200)<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">17:4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ñkpọ nte kilokram 2.3</char></note> akenọ anamusọ silfa, a-akedatta ammọ anam asen abasi. Ndin emaeben asen abasi ado ekewuuk ke ufọk Maika.<verse eid="JDG 17:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="JDG 17:5" />Ndin Maika amaanie ñwommo, ndin anye amaanam afọñ aboditọñ keed ye mme abasi ufọk ammọ anyʌñ atem ayịn amọ keed ke atu nditọ amọ nte aku. <verse eid="JDG 17:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JDG 17:6" />Ke ini ado Isrel ikinieghe adidem; afịd awo ekenam ñkpọ naña ammọ ekemama enyʌñ ekere ke anen.<verse eid="JDG 17:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="JDG 17:7" />Akparawa Lifai keed a-aketooho Betlehem ke Yuda, a-akesidʌññọ ke ubon Yuda, <verse eid="JDG 17:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JDG 17:8" />amaakpọñ abio Betlehem ke Yuda akeyem itie mfen se anye adʌñ. Ke usʌñ anye amaadiwakka ufọk Maika ke abod abio Ifrem.<verse eid="JDG 17:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="JDG 17:9" />Maika amaabịp anye, “Afo ato uke?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 17:9">Anye amaabọọrọ, “Ami ndo Lifai, nto Betlehem ke Yuda. Ami ñyeem itie nte ndʌñ.”<verse eid="JDG 17:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="JDG 17:10" />Ndin Maika amaabo anye ate, “Dʌñ ye ami nyʌñ do ete mmi ye aku, ndin ñyaunọ fiin sekel silfa duob<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">17:10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ñkpọ nte kram 115</char></note> ke isua, afọñ mfo ye ndidia mfo.” <verse eid="JDG 17:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JDG 17:11" />Ndin Lifai ado amaanyịmme adidʌñ ye anye, ndin akparawa ado amaakappa atie nte keed ke atu nditọ ideen amọ. <verse eid="JDG 17:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JDG 17:12" />Akem Maika amaanam Lifai ado akappa ado aku anyʌñ adʌñ ke ufọk amọ. <verse eid="JDG 17:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JDG 17:13" />Ndin Maika amaabo, “Idahami mmediọọñọ nte ke <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ayaafọn ye ami, sia Lifai ami adooho aku mmi.”<verse eid="JDG 17:13" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JDG 17" />
  <chapter number="18" style="c" sid="JDG 18" />
  <para style="s1">Mbon Daan Edʌñọ ke Lais</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JDG 18:1" />Ke ini ado Isrel ikinieghe adidem.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 18:1">Ndin ke ini ado esiin mbon Daan ekeyeem asaha itie ammọ se ammọ ekpedʌñọ, sia ammọ ikidʌkkọ udeeme ammọ diin ke atu mbon esiin Isrel. <verse eid="JDG 18:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JDG 18:2" />Ndin mbon Daan emaedọñ mme adadusʌñ ammọ awo ition eto Sora ye Estaol ekeyep isọñ enyʌñ ese naña anye aba. Mbon ami ekeka ke iwuod afịd mbon Daan. Ammọ emaedọkkọ ammọ ebo, “Ikaa ikise naña isọñ aba.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 18:2">Ndin ammọ emaedʌk ke abod abio Ifrem enyʌñ edi ke ufọk Maika, a-ammọ ekenaaha ke akonayio. <verse eid="JDG 18:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JDG 18:3" />Ke ini ammọ ekekpereke ufọk Maika, ammọ emaekop enyʌñ ediọọñọ uyio akparawa Lifai ado, ndin ammọ emaekanna iso edʌk enyʌñ ebịp anye, “Anie ikudat fiin idi mi? Nsoo ke afo anam ke ufọk ami? Ntak a-afo abaaha mmi-e?”<verse eid="JDG 18:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="JDG 18:4" />Anye amaadọkkọ ammọ se Maika akenam anọ anye, anyʌñ abo, “Anye amandat anam ami ndo aku amọ.”<verse eid="JDG 18:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="JDG 18:5" />Akem ammọ emaebo anye, “Mbọk bịp Abasi yak inie ifiọk mme isañ ñnyịn ayaaba ufọn.”<verse eid="JDG 18:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="JDG 18:6" />Aku ado amaabọọrọ ammọ, “Ikaa ke emem. Isañ ndufo ado se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaakenyịmme.”<verse eid="JDG 18:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="JDG 18:7" />Ndin ideen ition ado emaekpọñ enyʌñ edikas Lais, itie a-ammọ ekekịtte ete ke mme awo edʌñọ ke ifuuro, nte mbon Sidọn, ke emem ye ifuuro. Ndin sia isọñ ammọ imiikinanake ñkpọ, ammọ ekedo mbon uforo. Afen ñko, ammọ emaedʌñọ anyọọñ usʌñ akpọñ mbon Sidọn inyʌññọ inie ewuana ye awo ndomokeed.<verse eid="JDG 18:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="JDG 18:8" />Ke ini ammọ eketịmmeke enyọñ ekaa Sora ye Estaol, mbon Daan ammọ emaebịp ammọ, “Ndufo ekekịt die mme ñkpọ?”<verse eid="JDG 18:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="JDG 18:9" />Ammọ emaebọọrọ, “Idakka ida, yak ñnyịn inwana ye ammọ! Ñnyịn imaikịt isọñ ado, ndin anye ado ataa eti isọñ. Nte ndufo idiinamma ñkpọ ibaña? Ikiibiat ini adika do ñnyʌñ mben anye nnie. <verse eid="JDG 18:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JDG 18:10" />Ndufo emaekesịm do, ndufo eyaekịt mbon e-etieghe ke ndueidem ye akpa-akpa isọñ A-Abasi abenne isịn ndufo ke ubọk, isọñ afọnnọ inyʌññọ inana ñkpọ ndomokeed.”<verse eid="JDG 18:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="JDG 18:11" />Akem awo ikie itiokeed ke atu mbon Daan, emaebọbọ mbọbọekọñ, edaaña eto Sora ye Estaol. <verse eid="JDG 18:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JDG 18:12" />Ke usʌñ isañ ammọ emaenam itie nnaaekọñ ekpere Kiriad Yerịm ke Yuda. Ami ado ntak itie ado ke edem usobutịn Kiriad Yerịm akereke Mahaneh Daan<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">18:12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Mahaneh Daan awuọñọ atayad Daan</char></note> tutu mfịn ami. <verse eid="JDG 18:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JDG 18:13" />Ke itie ado ke ammọ ekedakka ekaa ke abod abio Ifrem enyʌñ edi ke ufọk Maika.<verse eid="JDG 18:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="JDG 18:14" />Akem awo ition e-ekekaaha ekeyep isọñ Lais ebo emọ-emọ mbon Daan ammọ, “Nte ndufo emediọọñọ ke keed ke atu mme ufọk ami a-anie afọñ aboditọñ, mme abasi ufọk ye usọ ubobodñkpọ keed e-edatta silfa enam? Idahami ndufo emediọọñọ se ekpenam.” <verse eid="JDG 18:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JDG 18:15" />Ndin ammọ emaekanna iso edọñọ do enyʌñ ekaa ufọk akparawa Lifai ke itie Maika emaenyʌñ ekọọm anye. <verse eid="JDG 18:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JDG 18:16" />Mbon Daan ikie itiokeed (600), e-ekebọbọke mbọbọekọñ, ekeda ke inuaatob. <verse eid="JDG 18:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JDG 18:17" />Mbon awo ition e-ekekaaha ekeyep isọñ edʌk ekaa enyʌñ ekeben isen abasi ado, afọñ aboditọñ ye mme abasi ufọk ke ini aku ye mbon ekọñ ikie itiokeed (600) ekedaaha ke inuaatob.<verse eid="JDG 18:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="JDG 18:18" />Ke ini awo ition ado ekedọọhọ eka ke ufọk Maika enyʌñ ekeben isen abasi ado, afọñ aboditọñ ye mme abasi ufọk, aku ado amaabịp ammọ, “Nsoo ke ndufo enam?”<verse eid="JDG 18:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="JDG 18:19" />Ammọ emaebọọrọ anye, “Kʌp Inua! Kuutañ ikọ ndomokeed. Ikeene ñnyịn nyʌñ do ete ye aku ñnyịn. Nte ifọnnọ afo adinam ñkpọ nnọọ esiin ye ubon ke Isrel nte aku akan ufọk awo keed kpọd?” <verse eid="JDG 18:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JDG 18:20" />Aku ado amaanem esịd eti-eti. Anye amaaben afọñ aboditọñ, mme abasi ufọk ye isen abasi anyʌñ adakka akeene mbon ado. <verse eid="JDG 18:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JDG 18:21" />Emaesio ñkeñe nditọ esịn ke iso, mme ufene ammọ ye mme inie ammọ, ammọ emaetịmme edem enyʌñ enyọñ.<verse eid="JDG 18:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="JDG 18:22" />Ke ini ammọ emaekekaa inyọọñ usʌñ ikpọñ ufọk Maika, emaekoot mme ideen awo e-ekedʌññọ ekpere Maika eboon ammọ itie keed, ammọ emaenyʌñ edibọhọ mbon Daan. <verse eid="JDG 18:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JDG 18:23" />Naña ammọ ekebọññọ ñkpo ekeene ammọ, mbon Daan emaekanna iso ebịp Maika, “Nsoo ido mfịna mfo nọ akoot ideen mfo yak edi anwan?”<verse eid="JDG 18:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="JDG 18:24" />Anye amaabọọrọ, “Ndufo emaeben mme abasi a-ami ñkenamma, ye aku mmi, enyʌñ edakka enyọñọ. Nsoo mfen ke ami nnie? Ndufo enam die ebịp, ‘Nsoo ido mfịna mfo?’ ”<verse eid="JDG 18:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="JDG 18:25" />Mbon Daan emaebọọrọ, “Kuufaaña ñkpọ ye ñnyịn, me idooho ndusʌk awo ekeme ediyat esịd enyʌñ etop ekọñ ye afo, ndin afo ye ufọk mfo eyaeduọọk uwem ndufo.” <verse eid="JDG 18:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="JDG 18:26" />Ndin mbon Daan emaedakka enyọñọ, ndin Maika, akekịt ke ammọ emaesọñ adudu ikan imọ, akanna iso anyʌñ atịmme anyọñ ufọk.<verse eid="JDG 18:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="JDG 18:27" />Akem ammọ emaeben se Maika akenam, ye aku amọ, edakka eka Lais, ebịne mbon e-ekebaaha ke emem ye ifuuro. Ammọ emaeketop ekọñ ke akañkañ enyʌñ efọp abio ammọ. <verse eid="JDG 18:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="JDG 18:28" />Ikibaaha awo se ikinwam ammọ sia ammọ ekedʌñọ ke anyan usʌñ ekpọñ Sidọn ndin inieghe ewuana ye awo ndomokeed. Abio ado akena ke itịkke ñkpere Bed Rehob.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 18:28">Mme mbon Daan emaetịmme ebọp abio ado enyʌñ edʌñọ do. <verse eid="JDG 18:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="JDG 18:29" />Ammọ emaekoot anye Daan ekeene eteete ammọ Daan, e-ekemanna enọ Isrel akpesʌkado ekesikoodo abio ado Lais. <verse eid="JDG 18:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="JDG 18:30" />Ke itie ado mme mbon Daan emaewuuk isen abasi enọ idem ammọ, ndin Yọnatan ayịn Kesọm, ayịn Moses, ye nditọ ammọ ekedoñño mme aku enọ esiin Daan tutu adisịm ke ini e-eketañña ammọ efep ke isọñ ado. <verse eid="JDG 18:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="JDG 18:31" />Ammọ emaekaa iso ekama ubobod abasi a-Maika akenamma, afịd ini ufọk Abasi akebaaha ke Silo.<verse eid="JDG 18:31" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JDG 18" />
  <chapter number="19" style="c" sid="JDG 19" />
  <para style="s1">Awo Lifai ye Anwaan Esa Amọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JDG 19:1" />Ke ini ado Isrel ikinieghe adidem.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 19:1">Ndin awo Lifai keed a-akedʌññọ ke esịd idʌñ keed ke abod abio Ifrem amaadat anwaan esa ke Betlehem ke Yuda. <verse eid="JDG 19:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JDG 19:2" />Ado anwaan esa ado ikinamma akpanikọ ye anye, amaasaña akpara. Anye amaakpọñ anye atịmme anyọñ abịne ete ye eka amọ ke Betlehem, Yuda. Anye amaakeba do ke afiọñ inaañ, <verse eid="JDG 19:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JDG 19:3" />ebe amọ amaakaa abịne anye akekpe ubọk yak anye atịmme adi. Anye akesaña ye ayịnufọk amọ ye dọñki iba. Anye amaaben anye adʌk ufọk ete ye eka amọ, ndin ke ini ete amọ akekịtte anye, anye amaadaara ke adidi amọ. <verse eid="JDG 19:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JDG 19:4" />Ukod amọ, ete awonwaan, amaatañ nọ anye aba do; ndin anye amaatie ye anye usen ita, ata anyʌñ anwọñ, anyʌñ adaiya idab do.<verse eid="JDG 19:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="JDG 19:5" />Ke ayọhọ usen inaañ ammọ emaebak edakka eda enyʌñ ebeeñe idem edinyọñ, ado ete awonwaan amaabo ebe ayịn amọ, “Sọọñọ idem mfo ke adidia etək ñkpọ; amaakem afo amekeme adinyọñ.” <verse eid="JDG 19:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JDG 19:6" />Ndin ammọ awo iba emaesuuk etie edia enyʌñ enwọñ ñkpọ itie keed. Ke emaekekweeñe ete awonwaan abo, “Mbọk tie ke akonayio ami nyʌñ bọ inemesịd.” <verse eid="JDG 19:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JDG 19:7" />Ndin awo ado akedakka ada ate inyọñ, ete anwaan amaakpeiye anye, ndin anye atie ke akonayio ado. <verse eid="JDG 19:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JDG 19:8" />Ke ubakusen ayọhọ usen ition, ke ini anye akedakkake ada adinyọñ, ete awonwaan amaabo, “Sọọñọ idem mfo. Bet tutu uweemeayio!” Ndin ammọ awo iba emaedia ñkpọ itie keed.<verse eid="JDG 19:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="JDG 19:9" />Akem ke ini awo ado, ye anwaan esa amọ ye ayịnufọk amọ, edaañake eda edinyọñọ, ukod amọ, ete awonwaan, abo, “Se idahami, akpere ndubiayio. Naa mi ke akonayio ami; usen aka adikweeñe. Tie nyʌñ nem idem mfo esịd. Ubakusen ñkpọñ afo amekeme adinyọñ idʌñ mfo.” <verse eid="JDG 19:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JDG 19:10" />Ado, sia ikiyemme aditie akonayio mfen, awo ado amaadakka anyʌñ asaña akaa usʌñ Yebus (a-adooho, Yeruselem), ye anwaan esa amọ ye mme dọñki iba e-ekebiommo mbiomo.<verse eid="JDG 19:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="JDG 19:11" />Ke ini ammọ ekekpereke Yebus ndin ayio akpere adikịm, ayịnufọk abo eteufọk amọ, “Di, yak ñnyịn itre ke abio mbon Yebus ami inyʌñ inaa mi ke akonayio.”<verse eid="JDG 19:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="JDG 19:12" />Eteufọk amọ amaabọọrọ ate, “Iyoo. Ñnyịn idiidʌkkọ ika ke abio ndomokeed ake mbon awo do imiidooho mbon Isrel. Ñnyịn idiika ko ke Kibie.” <verse eid="JDG 19:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JDG 19:13" />Anye amaadian, “Di, yak ñnyịn inwana isịm Kibie me Rama inyʌñ inaa do ke akonayio ke itie keed do.” <verse eid="JDG 19:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JDG 19:14" />Ndin ammọ emaekaa iso, utịn amaanyʌñ asop naña ammọ ekpereke Kibie ke Benyamin. <verse eid="JDG 19:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JDG 19:15" />Ke Kibie ke ammọ eketre nọ enaa do akonayio ado. Ammọ emaekaa eketie ke anwa abio, ado awo ndomokeed ikidatta amọ isịn ke ufọk ke akonayio ado.<verse eid="JDG 19:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="JDG 19:16" />Ke ndubiayio ado akaanadeen keed a-aketooho abod abio Ifrem, a-akedʌññọ ke Kibie (mbon se ikidʌñọ ke itie ado ekedoñño ubon Benyamin), ato inwañ anyọñ adi. <verse eid="JDG 19:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JDG 19:17" />Ke ini anye akeseeghe anyʌñ akịt akaisañ ado ke anwa abio, akaanadeen ado amaabịp, “Uke ke afo akaa? Uke ke afo aketo adi?”<verse eid="JDG 19:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="JDG 19:18" />Anye amaabọọrọ, “Ñnyịn ikito Betlehem ke Yuda ika ke esịd idʌñ keed ke abod abio Ifrem ake ami ndʌññọ. Ami ñkeba ke Betlehem ke Yuda ndin idahami ami ñka ufọk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. Ibaaha awo a-andatta miin adʌk ufọk ke akonayio ami. <verse eid="JDG 19:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JDG 19:19" />Ñnyịn iminie mmọọñ ye ñnyanyaha inọ dọñki ñnyịn ye uyo ye ukọd inọ idem ñnyịn nditọufọk mfo, ami, awonwaan ami ye akparawa a-abaaha ye ñnyịn. Ñnyịn iyemme ñkpọ ndomokeed.”<verse eid="JDG 19:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="JDG 19:20" />“Ami mmedaara ndufo edidi ke ufọk mmi,” akaanadeen ado amaabo. “Yak ami inọ se ndufo eyem. Ado ikiinaa ke anwa abio akonayio ami.” <verse eid="JDG 19:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JDG 19:21" />Ndin anye amaadat ammọ akaa ufọk amọ anyʌñ anọ dọñki ammọ ndidia. Ammọ emaekeyie ukod, emaenyʌñ edia ñkpọ enyʌñ enie se enwọñ.<verse eid="JDG 19:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="JDG 19:22" />Ke ini ammọ enọọhọ idem ammọ inemesịd, ndusʌk mbon ibak ke abio ado emaekanna ufọk ekʌk. Emaekpọkkọ usʌñ, ammọ emaebọñ ekoot akaanadeen andinie ufọk, “Sio awodeen a-akediighe ufọk mfo di nọ ñnyịn inam ima ye anye.”<verse eid="JDG 19:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="JDG 19:23" />Andinie ufọk ado amaawuọ aka akebo ammọ, “Iyoo, mme ufan mmi, ikiinam utọ idiọọk adinam ado. Sia awo ami ado asenawo mmi, ikiinam utọ mbubiam ido ami. <verse eid="JDG 19:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JDG 19:24" />Se, ayịn mmi awonwaan i-imiidiọọñọke awodeen akpa, ye anwaan esa amọ. Ami ñyaasio ammọ isọk ndufo idahami nọ ndufo enam se ema ye ammọ. Ado amaado awodeen ami, ikiinam utọ mbubiam ñkpọ ami.”<verse eid="JDG 19:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="JDG 19:25" />Ado mbon ado iyemme adikpañ utọñ nnọọ anye. Ndin awo ado amaaben anwaan esa amọ anyʌñ anọ ammọ ke anwa, ndin ammọ enaa anye ke ñkanubọk enyʌñ esappa anye ke afịd akonayio ado, ndin ke usiere ammọ eyaak anye anyọñ. <verse eid="JDG 19:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="JDG 19:26" />Ke usiere awonwaan ado amaatịmme anyọñ akaa ufọk e-eteufọk amọ akebaaha, aduọ ke anyenusʌñ anyʌñ anaa do tutu ayio anwaña.<verse eid="JDG 19:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="JDG 19:27" />Ke ini eteufọk amọ adakkake ada ke ubakusen anyʌñ abeere usʌñ ufọk asaña awuọ adika iso ke isañ amọ, se anwaan esa amọ do, amaaduọ ke inuausʌñ ufọk ado, ye ubọk amọ ke abai usʌñ. <verse eid="JDG 19:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="JDG 19:28" />Anye amaabo anye, “Dakka da; yak inyọñọ.” Ado ibọọrọ ikibaaha. Akem ete ado abenne anye atem ke anyọñ dọñki amọ anyʌñ anyọñ ufọk.<verse eid="JDG 19:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="JDG 19:29" />Ke ini anye asịmme ufọk, anye amaaben ikwa akpok anwaan esa amọ, ndido ke ndido, ke mbai duob mme iba anyʌñ anọ ammọ esọk afịd mme efaak ke Isrel. <verse eid="JDG 19:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="JDG 19:30" />Afịd awo se ikikịt ñkpọ ami emaebo emọ-emọ, “Utọ ñkpọ ado akenam awo ikịtte inyʌññọ inam, tọọñọ ke ini nditọ Isrel ekewuọhọ ke Iyib. Ikere ibaña! Ana nte ñnyịn inam ñkpọ! Ke ntoro isio uyio ndin!”<verse eid="JDG 19:30" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JDG 19" />
  <chapter number="20" style="c" sid="JDG 20" />
  <para style="s1">Mbon Isrel Emia Mme Ubon Benyamin Ufen</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JDG 20:1" />Akem afịd Isrel tọọñọ ke Daan tutu ke Beeseba ye ke isọñ Kilied emaedi ke itie keed enyʌñ eboho ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke Mispa. <verse eid="JDG 20:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JDG 20:2" />Mme adadusʌñ ke afịd esiin Isrel emaedat itie ammọ ke esob ikọd Abasi, awo tọsịn ikie inaañ (400,000) emaebọbọ mbọbọekọñ ye mme akañkañ. <verse eid="JDG 20:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JDG 20:3" />(Mme ubon Benyamin emaekop ke mbon Isrel emaedọọk ekaa ke Mispa.) Akem mbon Isrel emaebo, “Idọkkọ ñnyịn naña ñkpọ ndịk ami aketịppe.”<verse eid="JDG 20:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="JDG 20:4" />Ndin Lifai ado, ebe awonwaan e-ekewotto, amaabo, “Ami ye anwaan esa mmi ikidi ke Kibie ke Benyamin adina ke akonayio. <verse eid="JDG 20:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JDG 20:5" />Ke akonayio ideen Kibie emaembịne miin enyʌñ ekanna ufọk ekʌk, eyem ediñwot miin. Ammọ emaenaa anwaan esa mmi ke ñkanubọk, tutu anye akpa. <verse eid="JDG 20:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JDG 20:6" />Ami mmaaben anwaan esa mmi, mbak anye mbai-mbai ñnyʌñ mben mbai keedekeed nnọ esọk mme abio ke udeeme Isrel, sia ammọ ekenam ñkpọ asuenne ye mbubiam ñkpọ ami ke Isrel. <verse eid="JDG 20:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JDG 20:7" />Idahami, afịd ndufo mbon Isrel, isio uyio indọkkọ miin item se ndufo ebiere edinam.”<verse eid="JDG 20:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="JDG 20:8" />Afịd awo emaedaaña eda atọ keed ke uyio keed, ete, “Ñnyịn ndomokeed idiinyọññọ ufọk. Iyoo, ndomo awo keed ke atu ñnyịn idiinyọññọ ufọk amọ. <verse eid="JDG 20:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JDG 20:9" />Ado idahami se ñnyịn idiinam Kibie ado ami: Ñnyịn iyaidọọk ikaa ikinwana ye anye ke naña ukañ abiide. <verse eid="JDG 20:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JDG 20:10" />Ñnyịn iyaidat awo duob ke atu afịd ikie (100) ke afịd esiin Isrel, ye ikie keed (100) ke atu tọsịn keed (1,000), ye tọsịn keed (1,000) ke atu tọsịn duob (10,000), mbaak inie udia inọ mbon ekọñ. Amaakem, ke ini mbon ekọñ esịmme Kibie<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20:10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke ikpañwed Hibru enekke emaiwet Keba, asʌkkọ ado Kibie</char></note> ke Benyamin, anye ayaanọ ammọ se ammọ edot ke ñkpọ mbubiam ake ammọ enamma ke Isrel.” <verse eid="JDG 20:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JDG 20:11" />Ndin afịd mbon Isrel esoobo itie keed enyʌñ ediana keed enwana ye abio ado.<verse eid="JDG 20:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="JDG 20:12" />Mme esiin Isrel emaedọñ isʌñutom enọ afịd esiin Benyamin, ebo, “Nsoo utọ idiọọkñkpọ ndịk ke ekenam ami ke atu ndufo? <verse eid="JDG 20:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JDG 20:13" />Idahami iyaak mbon ibak ami ke Kibie inọ ñnyịn nọ iwoot ammọ inyʌñ isioño idiọọkñkpọ ke Isrel.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 20:13">Ado mme ubon Benyamin ikikpañña utọñ inọ emọ-emọ mbon Isrel ammọ. <verse eid="JDG 20:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JDG 20:14" />Ubon Benyamin emaeto ke mme abio ammọ ediboho itie keed ke Kibie edinwana ye mbon Isrel. <verse eid="JDG 20:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JDG 20:15" />Ini keed ini keed, ubon Benyamin emaemek mbon ukama akañkañ tọsịn edịb mme itiokeed (26,000) ke mme abio ammọ, edian ye mme akop idem ñkparawa ikie itiaba (700) ke atu mbon e-edʌñọke ke Kibie. <verse eid="JDG 20:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JDG 20:16" />Ke atu afịd mbon ekọñ e-ekesioho, ikie itiaba (700) ekedoñño mme atufiin, ammọ keedekeed e-ekeme editop itiad etọ ided ba keed ifeppe.<verse eid="JDG 20:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="JDG 20:17" />Isrel, ke amaaboiyo Benyamin, ekebat mbon ukama akañkañ tọsịn ikie inaañ (400,000), afịd ammọ emaenie ukeme edinwana ekọñ.<verse eid="JDG 20:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="JDG 20:18" />Mbon Isrel emaedọọk ekaa ke Beteel<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20:18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Akeme ido ufọk ake Abasi; se ñko ke Ñwed Mme Abiideikpe 20:26</char></note> enyʌñ ekebịp Abasi. Ammọ ekebo, “Anie ke atu ñnyịn abiido akpa adidọọk ñkaa ñkenwana ye ubon Benyamin?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 20:18">
    <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaabọọrọ abo, “Yuda ayaakaa akpa.”<verse eid="JDG 20:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="JDG 20:19" />Ke ubakusen mbon Isrel emaedaaña eda enyʌñ enam nnaaekọñ ekpere Kibie. <verse eid="JDG 20:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JDG 20:20" />Mbon Isrel emaewuọ ekaa edinwana ye ubon Benyamin enyʌñ edat itie ke iso ekọñ edinwana ammọ ke Kibie. <verse eid="JDG 20:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JDG 20:21" />Mbon Benyamin emaewuọñọ ke Kibie ediwoot mbon Isrel tọsịn edịb mme iba (22,000) ke iso ekọñ ke usen ado. <verse eid="JDG 20:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JDG 20:22" />Ado mbon Isrel emaenọ idem ammọ nsọọñọ idem ndin ini mfen etịmme edat itie ammọ ke itie a-ammọ e-ekedaahake idem ammọ akpa usen. <verse eid="JDG 20:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JDG 20:23" />Mbon Isrel emaedakka edọọk ekaa ekeseeme ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> tutu ndubiayio, ndin enyʌñ ebịp <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. Ammọ ekebo, “Nte ñnyịn itịmme idọọk ika ikinwana ye ubon Benyamin, emọ-emọ mbon Isrel ñnyịn?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 20:23">
    <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaabọọrọ ammọ, “Idọọk ikaa ikinwana ye ammọ.”<verse eid="JDG 20:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="JDG 20:24" />Akem mbon Isrel emaesịkke ekpere Benyamin ke ayọhọ usen iba. <verse eid="JDG 20:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JDG 20:25" />Ini ami, ke ini ubon Benyamin ekewuọñọke ke Kibie edi edinam ikọ ye ammọ, ammọ emaewot mbon Isrel awo tọsịn duob mme itiaita (18,000) mfen, afịd ammọ ye akañkañ.<verse eid="JDG 20:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="JDG 20:26" />Akem afịd mbon Isrel, atu mbon ekọñ, emaedọọk ekaa ke Beteel, ndin ke itie ado ammọ emaesuuk etie eseeme ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. Ammọ emaetie utreudia ke afịd usen ado tutu ndubiayio enyʌñ enam ufọfọb uwa ye uwa ewuana enọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. <verse eid="JDG 20:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="JDG 20:27" />Ndin mbon Isrel emaebịp <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> (Ke mme usen ado akebe edioomo Abasi mmọdo akeba, <verse eid="JDG 20:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="JDG 20:28" />ye Finehas ayịn Eliasa, ayịn Erọn, akesʌkkọ anam ñkpọ ke iso amọ.) Ammọ emaebịp, “Nte ñnyịn itịmme idọọk ika ikinwana ye ubon Benyamin, emọ-emọ mbon Isrel ñnyịn, mme ikuukaa?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 20:28">
    <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaabọọrọ ate, “Ikaa, sia ñkpọñ ami ñyaayaak ammọ isịn ke ubọk.”<verse eid="JDG 20:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="JDG 20:29" />Akem mbon Isrel emaenam nnaaekọñ ke ikọd ekanna Kibie ekʌk. <verse eid="JDG 20:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="JDG 20:30" />Mbon Isrel emaedakka edọọk ekaa ekenwana ye ubon Benyamin ke ayọhọ usen ita enyʌñ edat itie ammọ edinwana ye Kibie naña ekenam akpa. <verse eid="JDG 20:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="JDG 20:31" />Mme ubon Benyamin emaewuọ edi adisoobo ye ammọ ndin mbon Isrel emaedʌt ammọ ewuọ ekpọñ abio. Ammọ emaetọọñọ ediwoot mbon Isrel naña ekenam ke mme usen edem, ndin awo nte edịb mme duob emaekpañña ke usʌñ, ke akpọusʌñ a-akaaha Beteel mfen akaa Kibie. <verse eid="JDG 20:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="JDG 20:32" />Ke ini ubon Benyamin ekebooho, “Ñnyịn iyaikan ammọ nte ini akpa,” mbon Isrel ekesʌk ebo “Iyak ñnyịn itịmme edem inyʌñ idʌt ammọ iwuọ ke abio ika ke mme akpọusʌñ.”<verse eid="JDG 20:32" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="JDG 20:33" />Afịd mbon Isrel emaedakka ekpọñ itie ammọ enyʌñ ekedat mme itie ke Baal Tama, ndin mbon Isrel e-ekenaaha ke ikọd emaewuọ ekpọñ itie ammọ ke edem usobutịn Kibie.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20:33 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke usem Hibru ado Keba, asʌkkọ ado Kibie</char></note> <verse eid="JDG 20:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="JDG 20:34" />Akem tọsịn duob (10,000) mme anie ukeme ñkparawa Isrel emaewuọ ekaa iso ekenwana ye Kibie. Anwan ado amaasọñ tutu ubon Benyamin ikidiọọñọke ke nsobo anekke akpere. <verse eid="JDG 20:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="JDG 20:35" /><char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaakan Benyamin ke iso Isrel, ndin ke usen ado mbon Isrel emaewot awo tọsịn edịb mme ition ye ikie keed (25,100) ke ubon Benyamin, afịd emaebọbọ akañkañ ekọñ. <verse eid="JDG 20:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="JDG 20:36" />Ndin mme ubon Benyamin emaekịt ke ekan mmimọ.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 20:36">Akem mbon Isrel emaeyaak ufañ enọ Benyamin, sia ammọ ekedot anyen ke mbon a-ammọ ekenịmme nọ edịbe ke ikọd ekpere Kibie. <verse eid="JDG 20:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="JDG 20:37" />Mbon e-ekedịbeke ke ikọd emaewịppe ewuọ edọñọ Kibie, esuana enyʌñ edọñọ abio ndin emaewot afịd awo ke akañkañ. <verse eid="JDG 20:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="JDG 20:38" />Mbon Isrel emaedioomo ye mbon e-ekedịbeke ke ikọd ke ana nte ammọ enam ekamba ntuhube nsʌñikañ awuọ adọọk ke abio, <verse eid="JDG 20:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="JDG 20:39" />ndin amaakem mbon Isrel eyaebọọrọ ke anwan.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JDG 20:39">Ubon Benyamin emaetọọñọ ediwoot mbon Isrel (ñkpọ nte edịb mme duob), ndin ammọ emaebo, “Ñnyịn iyaikan ammọ kpa naña akedo ke akpa ekọñ.” <verse eid="JDG 20:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="JDG 20:40" />Ado ke ini eboho nsʌñikañ aketọọñọke adakka awuọ ke abio, ubon Benyamin emaekanna enyʌñ ekịt afịd abio naña adọọk anyọñ ke nsʌñikañ. <verse eid="JDG 20:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="JDG 20:41" />Akem mbon Isrel emaebọọrọ ke anwan, ndin ubon Benyamin emaekop ekamba ndịk, sia ammọ emaediọọñọ ke nsobo amaadisịm mmimọ. <verse eid="JDG 20:41" /><verse number="42" style="v" sid="JDG 20:42" />Ndin ammọ emaefeeñe ke iso mbon Isrel ekaa ke ñkañ anaan, ado ammọ ikikanna ibọkkọ ekọñ ado. Ndin mbon Isrel e-ekewuọñọke ke abio edi emaekpeeñe ammọ do. <verse eid="JDG 20:42" /><verse number="43" style="v" sid="JDG 20:43" />Ammọ emaekanna ubon Benyamin ekʌk, ebịne ammọ ikinyʌññọ isọsọñ ammọ adikan ammọ ubọk ke nsakiso Kibie ke edem usakkautịn. <verse eid="JDG 20:43" /><verse number="44" style="v" sid="JDG 20:44" />Mbon ubon Benyamin awo tọsịn duob mme itiaita (18,000) ekeduọññọ, afịd ammọ ekedo mbon uko ke ekọñ. <verse eid="JDG 20:44" /><verse number="45" style="v" sid="JDG 20:45" />Naña ammọ ekekanna iso efeeñe ekaa ke anaan ke itiad Rimọn, mbon Isrel emaekpeeñe awo tọsịn ition (5,000) eboon ke mben usʌñ. Ammọ esọọñọ efiik ubon Benyamin tutu ekesịm ke Kidọm enyʌñ emaana ewoot awo tọsịn iba (2,000) edian.<verse eid="JDG 20:45" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="46" style="v" sid="JDG 20:46" />Ke usen ado mbon ukama akañkañ Benyamin awo tọsịn edịb mme ition (25,000) ekeduọññọ, afịd ammọ ekedo mbon uko ke ekọñ. <verse eid="JDG 20:46" /><verse number="47" style="v" sid="JDG 20:47" />Ado awo ikie itiokeed (600) emaekanna iso efeeñe ekaa anaan ke itiad Rimọn, itie ake ammọ ekedʌññọ ke afiọñ inaañ. <verse eid="JDG 20:47" /><verse number="48" style="v" sid="JDG 20:48" />Mbon Isrel emaetịmme ekaa Benyamin enyʌñ ekesịn akañkañ ke afịd mme abio, ye mme unam ye afịd ñkpọ mfen ammọ ekekịtte. Afịd mme abio a-ammọ ekesañake, ammọ emaekịm ikañ esịn.<verse eid="JDG 20:48" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JDG 20" />
  <chapter number="21" style="c" sid="JDG 21" />
  <para style="s1">Ibaan Ndọ Ake Ubon Benyamin</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JDG 21:1" />Mme ideen ke Isrel emaeta unwọñọ ke Mispa ete: “Ibaaha awo ñnyịn ndomokeed ake adiinọ awo Benyamin ayịn awonwaan amọ ke ndọ.”<verse eid="JDG 21:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="JDG 21:2" />Mbon ami emaekaa Beteel,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">21:2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Akeme ido ekaufọk ake Abasi</char></note> itie a-ammọ eketieghe ke iso Abasi tutu ndubiayio, ebenne uyio ammọ enyʌñ etua ndod-ndod ayịd. <verse eid="JDG 21:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JDG 21:3" />Ammọ emaeseeme ebo, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, “Abasi Isrel, nsoo ido ntak a-ñkpọ ami aketịppeke anọ Isrel? Nsoo ido ntak e-esiin keed asoppo ke Isrel mfịn-e?”<verse eid="JDG 21:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="JDG 21:4" />Ke ubak-ubak usen edem usen mme awo ebọp akpokoro uwa enyʌñ enọ ufọfọb uwa ye uwa ewuana.<verse eid="JDG 21:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="JDG 21:5" />Akem mbon Isrel emaebịp ete, “Anie ke afịd esiin Isrel imiikibaaha ke esob ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>?” Sia ammọ emaekenịm unwọñọ ebaña awo ake idiidʌkkọ esob ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke Mispa ke akena nte ewot anye.<verse eid="JDG 21:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="JDG 21:6" />Ke ami mbon Isrel emaefʌhọ ebaña esiin Benyamin, mbon ammọ ke Isrel. Ammọ emaebo, “Mfịn e-ekpịkke esiin keed esio ke Isrel.” <verse eid="JDG 21:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JDG 21:7" />“Ñnyịn idiinam die inọ mbon se isʌhọ edọ ibaan, sia ñnyịn imaikinwọñọ ke anyịñ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke ñnyịn idiinọọhọ ammọ ndomo nditọ ibaan ñnyịn keed ke ndọ?” <verse eid="JDG 21:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JDG 21:8" />Akem ammọ emaebịp, “Akee esiin ke Isrel aketre adidʌk esob ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke Mispa?” Ammọ emaeyaara ediọọñọ ke awo ndomokeed ikitooho Yabes Kilied idi ke itie nnaa ke esob ado. <verse eid="JDG 21:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JDG 21:9" />Sia ke ini ammọ ekebatta awo, ammọ emaekịt ke awo ndomokeed ke Yabes Kilied ikibaaha do.<verse eid="JDG 21:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="JDG 21:10" />Ndin esob ado amaadọñ mbon ekọñ tọsịn duob mme iba (12,000) ye item ete eka ke Yabes Kilied enyʌñ ekama akañkañ ewot mbon se idʌñ do, ibaan ye ntəkayịn. <verse eid="JDG 21:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JDG 21:11" />Ammọ emaebo, “Ami ado se ana nte ndufo enam. Iwot afịd ideen ye afịd ibaan e-emaekesappa idem.” <verse eid="JDG 21:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JDG 21:12" />Ammọ emaekịt ke atu mbon e-edʌñọke ke Yabes Kilied ubọikpa ikie inaañ (400) a-adooho akenaanam inaaha ye awodeen, enyʌñ eben ammọ ekaa ke itie nnaaekọñ ke Silo ke Kenan.<verse eid="JDG 21:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="JDG 21:13" />Akem afịd esob edọñ enọ emem esọk ubon Benyamin ke itiad Rimọn. <verse eid="JDG 21:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JDG 21:14" />Ndin ubon Benyamin emaetịmme edi ke ini ado ndin emaenọ ammọ mme ibaan Yabes Kilied e-ekeyaaha uwem. Ado ammọ ikiwakka ikem afịd ammọ.<verse eid="JDG 21:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="JDG 21:15" />Mme awo emaefʌhọ ebaña Benyamin, sia <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaanam ufañ anaa ke mme esiin Isrel. <verse eid="JDG 21:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JDG 21:16" />Ndin mme ñkpisọñ ke esob emaebo, “Sia emaekesobo ibaan Benyamin, ñnyịn idiinam die inọ mme ideen e-ekesʌhọke ibaan? <verse eid="JDG 21:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JDG 21:17" />Ammọ emaebo, mme aduuwem ke ubon Benyamin ana nte enie mme adiaakpa,” “mbaak edisọọk esiin keed ke Isrel esio. <verse eid="JDG 21:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JDG 21:18" />Ñnyịn ikemeke adinọ ammọ nditọ ñnyịn ibaan ke ndọ, sia mbon Isrel emaeketa unwọñọ ami: ‘Adọdiọọk anọ awo ake anọọhọ awo ubon Benyamin anwaan.’ <verse eid="JDG 21:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JDG 21:19" />Ado se, usọrọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> aba ke afịd isua ke Silo, a-akenaaha ke adoro-adoro Beteel, ke usʌñ edem usakkautịn tọọñọ ke Beteel akaa Sekem, ye ke usuuk-usuuk Lebona.”<verse eid="JDG 21:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="JDG 21:20" />Ndin ammọ emaenọ ubon Benyamin item, ete, “Ikaa ikidịbe ke inwañ fain <verse eid="JDG 21:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JDG 21:21" />inyʌñ ikpeme. Ke ini mme ubọikpa Silo ewuọñọke edi edikeene enek unek, iwuọñọ ke inwañ fain ndin ndufo awo keedekeed imʌm keed ke atu ammọ yak ado anwaan mfo. Amaakem itịmme inyọñọ ikaa ke isọñ Benyamin. <verse eid="JDG 21:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JDG 21:22" />Ke ini mme ete ammọ me nditọeka ammọ ideen ediitañ ikọ inọọ ñnyịn, ñnyịn iyaibo ammọ, ‘Inam mfọn inọ ñnyịn ke adinwam ammọ, sia ñnyịn ikinọọhọ ammọ ibaan ke ini ekọñ. Ndufo idiidueghe ke edibiat ewʌhọ ndufo sia idooho ndufo ekenọọ ammọ mme nditọ ibaan ndufo.’ ”<verse eid="JDG 21:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="JDG 21:23" />Ndin kpa ado ke mme ubon Benyamin ekenam. Ke ini ubọikpa ado ekenekke unek, ideen keedekeed emaemʌm keed enyʌñ eben anye ewuọ nte anwaan amọ. Akem ammọ emaetịmme ekaa udeeme inie ammọ enyʌñ emaana ebọọp mme abio enyʌñ edʌñọ ke esịd.<verse eid="JDG 21:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="JDG 21:24" />Ke ini ado mbon Isrel emaekpọñ itie ado enyʌñ enyọñ ekaa idʌñ ammọ ke mme esiin ye ubon, keedekeed emaekaa udeeme inie amọ.<verse eid="JDG 21:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="JDG 21:25" />Ke mme usen ado Isrel ikinieghe adidem; afịd awo ekenam naña ekekịt ke anen.<verse eid="JDG 21:25" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JDG 21" />
</usx>